e":"Eisenhofer, Raphael","rank":41,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40910796"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/gigascience/giaf102","issn":["2047217X"],"journal":"GigaScience","paperid":"giaf102","status":"p","title":"GigaScience","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105015153714"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-800c0f14-aa19-4a37-a445-e22781d7e429"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Earth Hologenome Initiative : Data Release 1","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-829259","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Aims: Models predicting the likelihood of obstructive coronary artery disease (CAD) on invasive coronary angiography exist. However, as stable patients with new-onset chest pain frequently have lower clinical likelihood and preferably undergo index testing by non-invasive tests such as coronary computed tomography angiography (CCTA), clinical likelihood models calibrated against observed obstructive CAD at CCTA are warranted. The aim was to develop CCTA-calibrated risk-factor- and coronary artery calcium score-weighted clinical likelihood models (i.e. RF-CLCCTA and CACS-CLCCTA models, respectively). Methods and results: Based on age, sex, symptoms, and cardiovascular risk factors, an advanced machine learning algorithm utilized a training cohort (n = 38 269) of symptomatic outpatients with suspected obstructive CAD to develop both a RF-CLCCTA model and a CACS-CLCCTA model to predict observed obstructive CAD on CCTA. The models were validated in several cohorts (n = 28 340) and compared with a currently endorsed basic pre-test probability (Basic PTP) model. For both the training and pooled validation cohorts, observed obstructive CAD at CCTA was defined as >50% diameter stenosis. Observed obstructive CAD at CCTA was present in 6443 (22.7%) patients in the pooled validation cohort. While the Basic PTP underestimated the prevalence of observed obstructive CAD at CCTA, the RF-CLCCTA and CACS-CLCCTA models showed superior calibration. Compared with the Basic PTP model, the RF-CLCCTA and CACS-CLCCTA models showed superior discrimination (area under the receiver operating curves 0.71 [95% confidence interval (CI) 0.70-0.72] vs. 0.74 (95% CI 0.73-0.75) and 0.87 (95% CI 0.86-0.87), P < 0.001 for both comparisons). Conclusion: CCTA-calibrated clinical likelihood models improve calibration and discrimination of observed obstructive CAD at CCTA.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Laust Dupont","Schmidt, Samuel","Knuuti, Juhani","Spiro, Jon","Rajwani, Adil","Lopes, Pedro M","Lima, Maria Rita","Ferreira, António M","Maaniitty, Teemu","Saraste, Antti","Newby, David","Douglas, Pamela S","Bøttcher, Morten","Baskaran, Lohendran","Winther, Simon"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-792920"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Laust Dupont"],"country":["Australia","Finland","Portugal","Singapore","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Curtin University","Duke University","National Heart Centre Singapore","National University of Singapore","Royal Perth Hospital","Santa Cruz Hospital","Turku University Central Hospital","University of Edinburgh","University of Turku","University of Western Australia"],"keyword":["Aged","Calibration","Chronic coronary syndrome","Clinical likelihood","Cohort Studies","Computed Tomography Angiography","Computed Tomography Angiography methods","Coronary Angiography methods","Coronary Artery Disease diagnostic imaging","Coronary Stenosis diagnostic imaging","Coronary artery disease","Female","Humans","Likelihood Functions","Machine learning","Male","Middle Aged","Predictive Value of Tests","Retrospective Studies","Risk Assessment","Risk Factors","Severity of Illness Index"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Embargoed Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"clinical likelihood models calibrated against observed obstructive coronary artery disease on computed tomography angiography","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=105004050429&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The study was supported by The Danish Heart Foundation (grant no. 15-R99-A5837-22920), the Health Research Fund of Central Denmark Region, and Aarhus University Research foundation. The PROMISE trial was supported by grants from the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute (R01HL098237, R01HL098236, R01HL098305, and R01HL098235). L.D.R. acknowledges support from Danish Cardiovascular Academy (grant number PD5Y-2023001-DCA) which is funded by the Novo Nordisk Foundation (grant number NNF20SA0067242) and The Danish Heart Foundation. S.W. acknowledges support from the Novo Nordisk Foundation Clinical Emerging Investigator grant (NNF21OC0066981). L.B. acknowledges support from the National Medical Research Council (NMRC) of Singapore Centre (grant number CG21APR1006), and the NMRC of Singapore Transitional Award (grant number: TA21nov-0001). All other authors have nothing to declare. L.D.R. acknowledges support from Danish Cardiovascular Academy (grant number PD5Y-2023001-DCA) which is funded by the Novo Nordisk Foundation (grant number NNF20SA0067242) and The Danish Heart Foundation. S.W. acknowledges support from the Novo Nordisk Foundation Clinical Emerging Investigator grant (NNF21OC0066981). L.B. acknowledges support from the National Medical Research Council (NMRC) of Singapore Centre (grant number CG21APR1006), and the NMRC of Singapore Transitional Award (grant number: TA21nov-0001). All other authors have nothing to declare. The study was supported by The Danish Heart Foundation (grant no. 15-R99-A5837-22920), the Health Research Fund of Central Denmark Region, and Aarhus University Research foundation. The PROMISE trial was supported by grants from the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute (R01HL098237, R01HL098236, R01HL098305, and R01HL098235)."],"id":"S02-100.00-792920","identifier":[{"id":"PMC12042743","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"105004050429","t