{"abstract":"This chapter describes how to test different amyloid preparations for catalytic properties. We describe how to express, purify, prepare and test two types of pathological amyloid (tau and α-synuclein) and two functional amyloid proteins, namely CsgA from Escherichia coli and FapC from Pseudomonas. We therefore preface the methods section with an introduction to these two examples of functional amyloid and their remarkable structural and kinetic properties and high physical stability, which renders them very attractive for a range of nanotechnological designs, both for structural, medical and catalytic purposes. The simplicity and high surface exposure of the CsgA amyloid is particularly useful for the introduction of new functional properties and we therefore provide a computational protocol to graft active sites from an enzyme of interest into the amyloid structure. We hope that the methods described will inspire other researchers to explore the remarkable opportunities provided by bacterial functional amyloid in biotechnology.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Peña-Díaz, Samuel","Ferreira, Pedro","Ramos, Maria João","Otzen, Daniel E"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-744759"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Otzen, Daniel E"],"country":["Portugal"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Porto"],"keyword":["Amyloid chemistry","Amyloid formation","Bacterial Proteins chemistry","Catalysis","Catalytic Domain","Chromogenic substrates","Computational analysis","Escherichia coli Proteins metabolism","Escherichia coli genetics","Humans","Protein Engineering methods","Pseudomonas metabolism","QM MM","alpha Synuclein chemistry","tau Proteins metabolism"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mining and engineering activity in catalytic amyloids","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85190791654","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-744759","identifier":[{"id":"38816129","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85190791654","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-8843b42e-f8aa-4ac6-bd39-078baef4a0cd"],"keyword":["Amyloid formation","Amyloid/chemistry","Bacterial Proteins/chemistry","Catalysis","Catalytic Domain","Catalytic assays","Chromogenic substrates","Computational analysis","Escherichia coli Proteins/metabolism","Escherichia coli/genetics","Functional and pathological amyloid","Humans","Protein Engineering/methods","Pseudomonas/metabolism","QM/MM","alpha-Synuclein/chemistry","tau Proteins/metabolism"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9692A25E1F4DA968B61E0FB146973B63"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"pt","key":"university of porto","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Porto","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel","key":"peñadíazpau","last":"Peña-Díaz","locid":"ae060538-37cc-4b4e-a135-bcab499dafc6","name":"Peña-Díaz, Samuel","orcid":"0000-0002-2902-823X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro","key":"ferreirapau","last":"Ferreira","name":"Ferreira, Pedro","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria João","key":"ramospau","last":"Ramos","name":"Ramos, Maria João","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel E","key":"otzenpau","last":"Otzen","locid":"0ec06c22-1f74-4dd2-a894-af30b6565766","name":"Otzen, Daniel E","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38816129"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/bs.mie.2024.03.002","issn":["00766879","10792376"],"issn_org":["00766879"],"journal":"Methods in Enzymology","pages":"345-422","publisher":"Academic Press Inc.","status":"p","title":"Methods in Enzymology","volume":"697"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85190791654"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8843b42e-f8aa-4ac6-bd39-078baef4a0cd"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Mining and engineering activity in catalytic amyloids","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-744759","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This study investigates the geotechnical intricacies of Copenhagen's Quaternary upper clay till deposits, characterized as highly over-consolidated and significantly heterogeneous, and their impact on the structural performance of secant pile walls. Through rigorous analysis, 5000 samples were generated using multivariate distribution functions. These functions were developed to probabilistically calibrate the HS-small constitutive model, taking cross correlations into account. Additionally, 5000 more samples were generated assuming independence. These samples serve as the basis for a finite element model, providing crucial data on lateral wall deflections and bending moments. The impact of cross correlations among geotechnical properties on secant pile wall response is evident. The study quantifies this impact, showing a substantial reduction in standard deviation for lateral deflections (about 20%) compared to interdependent samples. The maximum bending moment during the final excavation stage sees a more modest 50% decrease. This study not only sheds light on the importance of considering dependencies among geotechnical properties in deep excavation design but also provides a practical framework for optimizing performance and safety in similar projects.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Panagiotis, Efthymios","Rocchi, Irene","Zania, Varvara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-759090"],"event":{"end":"2024-08-30","place":"Lisbon, pt","start":"2024-08-26","title":"ECSMGE 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Panagiotis, Efthymios"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"assessing the impact of correlated geotechnical properties on the behaviour of retaining structures","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1201/9781003431749-118","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-759090","ids":["dtu-678a1815-6b5d-4697-8371-3f158055bd77"],"keyword":["Cross correlations","Deep excavation design","Multivariate distribution functions","Secant pile walls"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-D8608E39BBD34094CAFE4256000FF0EB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/374651981/Pages_from_Geotechnical_Engineering_Challenges_to_Meet_Current_and_Emerging_Needs_of_Society_24_09_17_12_34_46-2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1201/9781003431749-118","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental and Resource Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental and Resource Engineering, Geotechnics & Geology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"E.","key":"panagiotispau","last":"Panagiotis","locid":"2509b949-d23f-4ed0-a9b2-f1d731fb0733","name":"Panagiotis, Efthymios","name_org":"Panagiotis, E.","orcid":"0000-0003-0806-0633","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"I.","key":"rocchipau","last":"Rocchi","locid":"8791c5f3-ce0c-418b-aa4f-25b8f9b45e60","name":"Rocchi, Irene","name_org":"Rocchi, I.","orcid":"0000-0003-0434-8031","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"V.","key":"zaniapau","last":"Zania","locid":"bd88e764-7eaa-4f3f-9b88-dac06731d808","name":"Zania, Varvara","name_org":"Zania, V.","orcid":"0000-0001-8270-1246","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nuno","key":"guerrapedh","last":"Guerra","name":"Guerra, Nuno","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Manuel Matos","key":"fernandespedh","last":"Fernandes","name":"Fernandes, Manuel Matos","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Cristiana","key":"ferreirapedh","last":"Ferreira","name":"Ferreira, Cristiana","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"António Gomes","key":"correiapedh","last":"Correia","name":"Correia, António Gomes","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Alexandre","key":"pintopedh","last":"Pinto","name":"Pinto, Alexandre","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Pedro","key":"sêcoepintopedh","last":"Sêco e Pinto","name":"Sêco e Pinto, Pedro","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1201/9781003431749-118","eisbn":["9781003431749"],"isbn":["9781032548166"],"pages":"719-722","publisher":"CRC Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the XVIII ECSMGE 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-678a1815-6b5d-4697-8371-3f158055bd77"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Assessing the impact of correlated geotechnical properties on the behaviour of retaining structures","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-759090","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The bearing capacity of soils is critical for the design and analysis of foundations. The classical solutions derived from methods of characteristics and bound theories are based on the rigid plasticity and associated flow rule, which may not be realistic for natural soils. The undrained shear strength of soft clays exhibits strain-softening and anisotropic behavior in the lab tests, which creates complexity to choose appropriate strength parameters in conventional design process. In addition, the stress-strain characters are non-associative and path dependent, which also affects the bearing capacity of soils. This paper investigates one classical stability problem (i.e. deeply-embedded pile/pipe section) using the finite element analysis and MIT-E3 soil model, and demonstrates the effects of strain-softening and strength anisotropy on the undrained resistance of soils. The computed results are compared with analytical solutions and finite element limit analysis. These findings have strong practical implications to predict the bearing capacity of foundations and interpret insitu tests.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Dong, Yuepeng"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-759158"],"event":{"end":"2024-08-30","place":"Lisbon, pt","start":"2024-08-26","title":"ECSMGE 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Strain softening"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of strain softening and strength anisotropy on the undrained resistance of deeply embedded pile pipe section","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1201/9781003431749-62","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-759158","ids":["dtu-870f4f95-97db-4ea2-9910-46915d9d2498"],"keyword":["Bearing capacity of soils","Strain-softening","Strength anisotropy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-B95176090019B4FC7335F527B95EB814"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1201/9781003431749-62","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/374652321/Pages_from_Geotechnical_Engineering_Challenges_to_Meet_Current_and_Emerging_Needs_of_Society_24_09_17_12_34_46.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental and Resource Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental and Resource Engineering, Geotechnics & Geology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Y. P.","key":"dongpau","last":"Dong","locid":"1a3b4d77-452f-4099-98c4-611efe3f290c","name":"Dong, Yuepeng","name_org":"Dong, Y. P.","orcid":"0000-0003-2577-4814","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nuno","key":"guerrapedh","last":"Guerra","name":"Guerra, Nuno","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Manuel Matos","key":"fernandespedh","last":"Fernandes","name":"Fernandes, Manuel Matos","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Cristiana","key":"ferreirapedh","last":"Ferreira","name":"Ferreira, Cristiana","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"António Gomes","key":"correiapedh","last":"Correia","name":"Correia, António Gomes","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Alexandre","key":"pintopedh","last":"Pinto","name":"Pinto, Alexandre","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Pedro","key":"sêcoepintopedh","last":"Sêco e Pinto","name":"Sêco e Pinto, Pedro","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1201/9781003431749-62","eisbn":["9781003431749"],"isbn":["9781032548166"],"pages":"456-461","publisher":"CRC Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the XVIII ECSMGE 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-870f4f95-97db-4ea2-9910-46915d9d2498"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Effect of strain-softening and strength anisotropy on the undrained resistance of deeply embedded pile/pipe section","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-759158","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Screw piles have been the subject of extensive research, with various methodologies proposed to predict installation torque from earth pressure theory-based and Cone Penetration Test (CPT)-based perspectives. Accurate prediction of installation torque is crucial for determining the required equipment, assessing the suitability of screw piles as a foundation solution, and ensuring that the pile material does not yield under the installation torque necessary for a specific installation depth. This study aims to modify existing methods and adapt them to the unique geometry of the screw piles investigated at Aalborg University. The methodologies compared in this study are based on experiments in saturated sand carried out at the laboratories at Aalborg University. The results indicate that earth pressure theory-based approaches provide more consistent outcomes, while CPT-based methods exhibit greater scatter. Consequently, it is concluded that current methods for predicting installation torque are unreliable, necessitating further research.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Andreasen, Daniel Kristian","Ibsen, Lars Bo","Koteras, Aleksandra Katarzyna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-762247"],"event":{"end":"2024-08-30","place":"Lisbon, pt","start":"2024-08-26","title":"ECSMGE 24","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Analytical methods","CPT","CPT based methods","Earth pressure","Experiments","Screw piles"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evaluating the reliability of existing methods for predicting installation torque of screw piles in saturated sand a comparative study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1201/9781003431749-32","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-762247","ids":["aau-5497d984-3e8c-4207-9730-6c95cbee622c"],"keyword":["Analytical methods","CPT","CPT-based methods","Earth pressure","Experiments","Screw piles"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-4628D37AF2F936E53770070A9BC6D502"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/762594108/Evaluating_the_reliability_of_existing_methods_for_predicting_installation_torque_of_screw_piles_in_saturated_sand_a_comparative_study_25_01_15_08_58_18.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/746923721/Evaluating_the_reliability_of_existing_methods_for_predict.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1201/9781003431749-32","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Structures, Geotechnics and Risk","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Geotechnical Engineering and Offshore Foundations Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel Kristian","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"cd6949ad-ae79-4c1f-99a9-72c2afeeed3f","name":"Andreasen, Daniel Kristian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Bo","key":"ibsenpau","last":"Ibsen","locid":"23b734a4-b2f7-44cd-ba17-e812ddc3640c","name":"Ibsen, Lars Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-1304-6660","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Aleksandra Katarzyna","key":"koteraspau","last":"Koteras","locid":"a7438315-bb6a-4efa-b4d3-d48fda2ab067","name":"Koteras, Aleksandra Katarzyna","orcid":"0000-0001-5761-807X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nuno","key":"guerrapedh","last":"Guerra","name":"Guerra, Nuno","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Manuel","key":"matosfernandespedh","last":"Matos Fernandes","name":"Matos Fernandes, Manuel","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Cristiana","key":"ferreirapedh","last":"Ferreira","name":"Ferreira, Cristiana","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"António","key":"gomescorreiapedh","last":"Gomes Correia","name":"Gomes Correia, António","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Alexandre","key":"pintopedh","last":"Pinto","name":"Pinto, Alexandre","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Pedro","key":"sêcoepintopedh","last":"Sêco e Pinto","name":"Sêco e Pinto, Pedro","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1201/9781003431749-32","edition":"1st Edition","eisbn":["9781003431749"],"isbn":["9781032548166"],"pages":"315-319","place":"London","publisher":"CRC Press","status":"p","subtitle":"PROCEEDINGS OF THE XVIII EUROPEAN CONFERENCE ON SOIL MECHANICS AND GEOTECHNICALENGINEERING","title":"Geotechnical Engineering Challenges to Meet Current and Emerging Needs of Society"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["12. Responsible Consumption and Production","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg Universit