{"abstract":"Many platforms host user-generated content (UGC) and content developed by professionals side by side. However, thus far, their impact on platform ecosystems has been mostly studied in isolation. In this paper, we use data from a network of 122 local news outlets hosted by an online news platform to study the spillover effects from UGC developed by citizen journalists to the content developed by professional journalists. We use the removal of a status index associated with citizen journalists as an exogenous shock to their supply of UGC to identify these spillover effects. We find that experienced citizen journalists reduce their production of content when this status index is removed. We then find that inexperienced professional journalists increase their output in response to this behavior. However, as a result of these changes, we find a reduction in the overall content hosted by the platform, especially in the case of local news and in more isolated regions. We further show that this is likely to have detrimental effects for the platform. In particular, there is a decline in overall viewership, and the platform may need to hire and pay salaries to more professional journalists to produce enough articles to close the gap left by the departing citizen journalists. Our work contributes to the literature on UGC and online platforms and to the literature on local news.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Sen, Ananya","Grad, Tom","Ferreira, Pedro","Claussen, Jörg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-700489"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Grad, Tom"],"country":["Germany","Portugal","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Carnegie Mellon University","Ludwig-Maximillians-Universität Munich","Nova School of Business and Economics"],"keyword":["Local news","Platforms","Professionals","User generated content"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how does user generated content impact content generated by professionals evidence from local news","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/101424635/ananya_sen_et_al_how_does_user-generated_content_acceptedversion.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-700489","identifier":[{"id":"85203137806","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-8ea4aca6-2c59-4f48-8dd7-a6bb69372fb7"],"keyword":["Local news","Platforms","Professionals","User-generated content"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-00DA4856DD7CD5308C8D5D2AF6AEBE28"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/101424635/ananya_sen_et_al_how_does_user-generated_content_acceptedversion.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"carnegie mellon university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Carnegie Mellon University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Strategy and Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"pt","key":"nova school of business and economics","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Nova School of Business and Economics","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"ludwig maximillians universität munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ludwig-Maximillians-Universität Munich","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ananya","key":"senpau","last":"Sen","name":"Sen, Ananya","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tom","key":"gradpau","last":"Grad","locid":"dbb18f05-026e-4604-9cbf-7a1e150d27c5","name":"Grad, Tom","orcid":"0000-0003-0528-173X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro","key":"ferreirapau","last":"Ferreira","name":"Ferreira, Pedro","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jörg","key":"claussenpau","last":"Claussen","locid":"28989f02-fc99-463e-a60a-c857199c7771","name":"Claussen, Jörg","orcid":"0000-0001-8432-8860","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1287/mnsc.2023.4962","issn":["00251909","15265501"],"issn_org":["00251909"],"issue":"9","journal":"Management Science","pages":"6045-6068","publisher":"INFORMS Institute for Operations Research and the Management Sciences","status":"p","title":"Management Science","volume":"70"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85203137806"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-8ea4aca6-2c59-4f48-8dd7-a6bb69372fb7"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"(How) Does User-generated Content Impact Content Generated by Professionals? : Evidence From Local News","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-700489","year":"2024","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Speothos pacivorus is an extinct South American canid (Canidae: Cerdocyonina) from the Pleistocene of Lagoa Santa Karst, Central Brazil. This taxon is one of the hypercarnivore canids that vanished from the continent at the end of Pleistocene. Although all remains of Speothos pacivorus were collected in the 19th century by the Danish naturalist Peter W. Lund, few studies have committed to an in-depth analysis of the taxon and the known specimens. Here, we analyzed all biological remains of S. pacivorus hosted in the Peter Lund/Quaternary Collection at the Natural History Museum of Denmark, Copenhagen, by listing and illustrating all its specimens known to date. We also conducted a reconstruction of the holotype, an almost complete cranium, based on a µCT scan, producing an undeformed and crack-free three-dimensional model. With this data available we aim to foster new research on this elusive species.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Ruiz, Juan V.","Kyriakouli, Christina","Hansen, Kasper Lykke","Gundlach, Carsten","Ferreira, Gabriel S.","Machado, Fabio A.","Godoy, Pedro L.","Castro, Mariela C.","Montefeltro, Felipe C."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-738789"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","America, South","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Brazil","Germany","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Federal University of Goiás","Oklahoma State University","Stony Brook University","Universidade de São Paulo","University of Tübingen"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the fossils of i speothos pacivorus i carnivora canidae at the peter lund quaternary collection of the natural history museum of denmark","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"d