 and Geotechnical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"cowi","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-COWI","l3nl":"COWI A/S","l3nn":"COWI","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"COWI","namevar":["COWI A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-COWI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J.Z.","key":"krabbepau","last":"Krabbe","name":"Krabbe, J.Z.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kenny Kataoka","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"62a8cfd4-8bb4-4146-b3e9-60fc72605838","name":"Sørensen, Kenny Kataoka","orcid":"0000-0001-9400-7753","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"M.R.","key":"lodahlpau","last":"Lodahl","name":"Lodahl, M.R.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nuno","key":"guerrapedh","last":"Guerra","name":"Guerra, Nuno","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Manuel","key":"matosfernandespedh","last":"Matos Fernandes","name":"Matos Fernandes, Manuel","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Cristiana","key":"ferreirapedh","last":"Ferreira","name":"Ferreira, Cristiana","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"António","key":"gomescorreiapedh","last":"Gomes Correia","name":"Gomes Correia, António","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Alexandre","key":"pintopedh","last":"Pinto","name":"Pinto, Alexandre","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Pedro","key":"sêcopintopedh","last":"Sêco Pinto","name":"Sêco Pinto, Pedro","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"1","eisbn":["9781003431749"],"place":"London","publisher":"CRC Press","status":"p","title":"Geotechnical Engineering Challenges to Meet Current and Emerging Needs of Society"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","COWI A/S","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","NIRAS A/S","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-33a8ce26-bff8-4920-b778-5a90194ba96d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Effects of physical characteristics on the shear behaviour of Foulum glaciofluvial sand","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-772067","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"It has been suggested that substance use disorders could lead to accelerated biological aging, but only a few neuroimaging studies have investigated this hypothesis so far. In this cross-sectional study, structural neuroimaging was performed to measure cortical thickness (CT) in tricenarian adults with cocaine use disorder (CUD, n1 = 30) and their age-paired controls (YC, n1 = 30), and compare it with octogenarian elder controls (EC, n1 = 20). We found that CT in the right fusiform gyrus was similar between CUD and EC, thinner than the expected values of YC. We also found that regarding CT of the right inferior temporal gyrus, right inferior parietal cortex, and left superior parietal cortex, the CUD group exhibited parameters that fell in between EC and YC groups. Finally, CT of the right pars triangularis bordering with orbitofrontal gyrus, right superior temporal gyrus, and right precentral gyrus were reduced in CUD when contrasted with YC, but those areas were unrelated to CT of EC. Despite the 50-year age gap between our age groups, CT of tricenarian cocaine users assembles features of an octogenarian brain, reinforcing the accelerated aging hypothesis in CUD.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Rothmann, Leonardo Melo","Tondo, Lucca Pizzato","Borelli, Wyllians Vendramini","Esper, Nathalia Bianchini","Portolan, Eduardo Tavares","Franco, Alexandre Rosa","Portuguez, Mirna Wetters","Ferreira, Pedro Eugênio","Bittencourt, Augusto Martins Lucas","Soder, Ricardo Bernardi","Viola, Thiago Wendt","da Costa, Jaderson Costa","Grassi-Oliveira, Rodrigo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-807713"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","America, South","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Grassi-Oliveira, Rodrigo"],"country":["Brazil","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Child Mind Institute, Inc.","Nathan S. Kline Institute for Psychiatric Research","New York Univers