":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85206895177"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f261c360-f117-4f98-9961-b659ccadff03","ku-15f42ef6-c79e-43d4-aa88-aeeac32ea99c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The global distribution and drivers of wood density and their impact on forest carbon stocks","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-785242","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Objective: The cingulate gyrus is implicated in the neurobiology of addiction, such as chronic cocaine consumption. Early-life stress (ELS) is an important moderator of cocaine use disorder (CUD). Therefore, we investigated the effect of CUD on cingulate cortical thickness and tested whether a history of ELS could influence the effects of CUD. Methods: Participants aged 18 to 50 years (78 with CUD due to crack cocaine consumption and 53 healthy controls) underwent MRI and the cingulate thickness (rostral anterior, caudal anterior, posterior, and isthmus regions) was analyzed. The clinical assessment comprised the Childhood Trauma Questionnaire (CTQ) and the Addiction Severity Index. Group comparisons adjusting by sex, age, and education were performed. Mediation models were generated where lifetime cocaine use, CTQ score, and cortical thickness corresponded to the independent variable, intermediary variable, and outcome, respectively. Results: Group comparisons revealed significant differences in six out of eight cingulate cortices, showing lower thickness in the CUD group. Furthermore, years of regular cocaine use was the variable most associated with cingulate thickness. Negative correlations were found between CTQ scores and the isthmus cingulate (right hemisphere), as well as with the rostral anterior cingulate (left hemisphere). In the mediation analysis, we observed a significant negative direct effect of lifetime cocaine use on the isthmus cingulate and an indirect effect of cocaine use mediated by CTQ score. Conclusion: Our findings suggest that a history of ELS could aggravate the negative effects of chronic cocaine use on the cingulate gyrus, particularly in the right isthmus cingulate cortex.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Bittencourt, Augusto Martins Lucas","Belmonte Da Silveira, Bárbara Luiza","Tondo, Lucca Pizzato","Melo Rothmann, Leonardo","Rosa Franco, Alexandre","Ferreira, Pedro Eugenio Mazzucchi Santana","Viola, Thiago Wendt","Grassi-Oliveira, Rodrigo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-187060"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","America, South","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Grassi-Oliveira, Rodrigo"],"country":["Brazil","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Child Mind Institute, Inc.","Nathan S. Kline Institute for Psychiatric Research","New York University","Pontificia Universidade Catolica do Rio Grande do Sul","Universidade Catolica de Pelotas"],"keyword":["Adverse childhood experiences","Child Abuse","Cocaine Related Disorders","Crack Cocaine","Gyrus Cinguli diagnostic imaging","Humans","Magnetic Resonance Imaging methods","Neuroimaging","Psychological Tests","Self Report"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cingulate cortical thickness in cocaine use disorder mediation effect between early life stress and cocaine consumption","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85143059417","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-187060","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10203054","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"36416534","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85143059417","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-65100979-2d8b-4fe4-8408-639a1054a470"],"keyword":["Adverse Childhood Experiences","Child Abuse","Cocaine-Related Disorders","Cocaine-Related Disorders/diagnostic imaging","Crack Cocaine","Gyrus Cinguli","Gyrus Cinguli/diagnostic imaging","Humans","Magnetic Resonance Imaging/methods","Neuroimaging","Psychological Tests","Self Report"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D9489682E9D9468BDC15AB5EC72097C2"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"br","key":"pontificia universidade catolica do rio grande do sul","loc":["Brazil","America, South"],"name":"Pontificia Universidade Catolica do Rio Grande do Sul","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"br","key":"universidade catolica de pelotas","loc":["Brazil","America, South"],"name":"Universidade Catolica de Pelotas","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"nathan s kline institute for psychiatric research","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Nathan S. Kline Institute for Psychiatric Research","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"child mind institute inc","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Child Mind Institute, Inc.","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"new york university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"New York University","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Translational Neuropsychiatry Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Augusto Martins Lucas","key":"bittencourtpau","last":"Bittencourt","name":"Bittencourt, Augusto Martins Lucas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bárbara Luiza","key":"belmontedasilveirapau","last":"Belmonte Da Silveira","name":"Belmonte Da Silveira, Bárbara Luiza","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lucca Pizzato","key":"tondopau","last":"Tondo","name":"Tondo, Lucca Pizzato","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leonardo","key":"melorothmannpau","last":"Melo Rothmann","name":"Melo Rothmann, Leonardo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexandre","key":"rosafrancopau","last":"Rosa Franco","name":"Rosa Franco, Alexandre","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro Eugenio Mazzucchi Santana","key":"ferreirapau","last":"Ferreira","name":"Ferreira, Pedro Eugenio Mazzucchi Santana","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thiago Wendt","key":"violapau","last":"Viola","name":"Viola, Thiago Wendt","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 6","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rodrigo","key":"grassioliveirapau","last":"Grassi-Oliveira","locid":"fa6d6df6-793a-4406-96e1-cd40f0604227","name":"Grassi-Oliveira, Rodrigo","orcid":"0000-0001-9911-5921","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36416534"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1017/neu.2022.33","issn":["09242708","16015215"],"issn_org":["09242708"],"issue":"2","journal":"Acta Neuropsychiatrica","pages":"78-86","publisher":"Cambridge University Press","status":"p","title":"Acta Neuropsychiatrica","volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85143059417"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-65100979-2d8b-4fe4-8408-639a1054a470"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Cingulate cortical thickness in cocaine use disorder : Mediation effect between early life stress and cocaine consumption","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-187060","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Obesity entails metabolic alterations across multiple organs, highlighting the role of inter-organ communication in its pathogenesis. Extracellular vesicles (EVs) are communication agents in physiological and pathological conditions, and although they have been associated with obesity comorbidities, their protein cargo in this context remains largely unknown. To decipher the messages encapsulated in EVs, we isolated plasma-derived EVs from a diet-induced obese murine model. Obese plasma EVs exhibited a decline in protein diversity while control EVs revealed significant enrichment in protein-folding functions, highlighting the importance of proper folding in maintaining metabolic homeostasis. Previously, we revealed that gut-derived EVs’ proteome holds particular significance in obesity. Here, we compared plasma and gut EVs and identified four proteins exclusively present in the control state of both EVs, revealing the potential for a non-invasive assessment of gut health by analyzing blood-derived EVs. Given the relevance of post-translational modifications (PTMs), we observed a shift in chromatin-related proteins from glycation to acetylation in obese gut EVs, suggesting a regulatory mechanism targeting DNA transcription during obesity. This study provides valuable insights into novel roles of EVs and protein PTMs in the intricate mechanisms underlying obesity, shedding light on potential biomarkers and pathways for future research.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Baptista Pereira, Pedro","Torrejón, Estefania","Ferreira, Inês","Carvalho, Ana Sofia","Teshima, Akiko","Sousa-Lima, Inês","Beck, Hans Christian","Costa-Silva, Bruno","Matthiesen, Rune","Macedo, Maria Paula","de Oliveira, Rita Machado"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-733909"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Macedo, Maria Paula","de Oliveira, Rita Machado"],"country":["Portugal"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Fundação Champalimaud","NOVA University Lisbon"],"keyword":["Extracellular vesicles","Metabolism","Obesity","Post translational modifications","Prediabetes","Protein glycation","Proteomics"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"proteomic profiling of plasma and gut derived extracellular vesicles in obesity","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/nu16050736","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This research was funded by Fundação para a Ciência e a Tecnologia (PTDC/MEC-MET/29314/2017, and 2022.05764.PTDC), by the European Comission CORDIS Pas Gras Project (101080329) and by the European Union EVCA Twining Project (Horizon GA n° 101079264)."],"id":"S01-000.00-733909","identifier":[{"id":"38474865","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10935251","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85187483516","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-7e9dfc4c-c2d2-4ba1-89df-0392518cbc1a"],"keyword":["extracellular vesicles","metabolism","obesity","post-translational modifications","prediabetes","protein acetylation","protein glycation","proteomics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6E4A324B9F591D9EA94A33B34B65E580"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/nu16050736","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/257310684/nutrients-16-00736.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"pt","key":"nova university lisbon","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"NOVA University Lisbon","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Biochemistry (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"pt","key":"fundação champalimaud","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Fundação Champalimaud","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro","key":"baptistapereirapau","last":"Baptista Pereira","name":"Baptista Pereira, Pedro","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Estefania","key":"torrejónpau","last":"Torrejón","name":"Torrejón, Estefania","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Inês","key":"ferreirapau","last":"Ferreira","name":"Ferreira, Inês","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ana Sofia","key":"carvalhopau","last":"Carvalho","name":"Carvalho, Ana Sofia","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Akiko","key":"teshimapau","last":"Teshima","name":"Teshima, Akiko","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Inês","key":"sousalimapau","last":"Sousa-Lima","name":"Sousa-Lima, Inês","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans Christian","key":"beckpau","last":"Beck","locid":"93687fda-7a9e-4e81-8cf0-49cc73c0fe73","name":"Beck, Hans Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-7763-3637","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Bruno","key":"costasilvapau","last":"Costa-Silva","name":"Costa-Silva, Bruno","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune","key":"matthiesenpau","last":"Matthiesen","name":"Matthiesen, Rune","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Paula","key":"macedopau","last":"Macedo","name":"Macedo, Maria Paula","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rita Machado","key":"deoliveirapau","last":"de Oliveira","name":"de Oliveira, Rita Machado","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38474865"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/nu16050736","issn":["20726643"],"issue":"5","journal":"Nutrients","paperid":"736","publisher":"MDPI","status":"p","title":"Nutrients","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85187483516"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-7e9dfc4c-c2d2-4ba1-89df-0392518cbc1a"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Proteomic Profiling of Plasma- and Gut-Derived Extracellular Vesicles in Obesity","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-733909","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"ICT4D has increasingly adopted participation and community involvement to address power imbalances, namely through the figure of the \"local\". However, this reliance makes assumptions about the nature of the \"local\" while limiting scrutiny of research approaches. Through a Postcolonial Critical Discourse Analysis, this paper argues that 1) communities are often essentialized in agency-depriving ways, 2) researchers claim substantial discretionary power in representing communities, and 3) participatory approaches are framed as inherently beneficial, obscuring compromises. The analysis suggests participation serves to maintain the status quo. Going forward, ICT4D research should ground claims in evidence, demonstrate community benefits, acknowledge complexities transparently, and question premises that empirical gaps alone justify research. Rather than participation as a panacea, a reflexive ICT4D should scrutinize representational practices and notions of empowerment that may perpetuate inequities.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Ferreira, Pedro"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747271"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Community involvement","Discretionary power","ICT4D","Participatory Approaches","Postcolonial Critical Discourse Analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"examining the local in ict000000000004d a postcolonial perspective on participation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3613904.3642748","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747271","identifier":[{"id":"85194816444","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-fca3944c-1e1e-4a1e-b18d-6da6f84e8c75"],"keyword":["Community Involvement","Discretionary Power","ICT4D","Participatory Approaches","Postcolonial Critical Discourse Analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-09DA091789E19EB4504BA5F4909D5C82"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3613904.3642748","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, ETHOS Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro","key":"ferreirapau","last":"Ferreira","locid":"1b3cff7f-1549-4998-b52e-0ba9093e1d01","name":"Ferreira, Pedro","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3613904.3642748","pages":"1-13","status":"p","title":"CHI '24: Proceedings of the CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85194816444"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-fca3944c-1e1e-4a1e-b18d-6da6f84e8c75"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Examining the \"Local\" in ICT4D : A Postcolonial Perspective on Participation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747271","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Accurate determination of bearing capacity for screw piles remains an unresolved challenge. Previous research has predominantly concentrated on uplift capacity equations for helical anchors, with limited focus on compression capacity. This study aims to assess and adapt existing methodologies for determining the bearing capacity of screw piles, accounting for the distinct geometrical features, and applying them to both uplift and compression capacities. Additionally, Cone Penetration Test (CPT)-based methods are investigated for their applicability in this context. The research methodology entails reviewing current bearing capacity determination methods, modifying them to accommodate the unique screw pile geometry, and analysing CPT-based approaches. Static load tests are conducted at Aalborg University's laboratory to obtain reference static bearing capacities. Comparisons are drawn between the outcomes of the adapted earth pressure theory-based and CPT-based methods and the lab-obtained static bearing capacities. The results indicate that the existing framework is inadequate and unreliable for determining the uplift and compression bearing capacity of the screw piles investigated. The study highlights the necessity for further research and development of novel methodologies to enhance the accuracy of screw pile bearing capacity predictions.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Andreasen, Daniel Kristian","Koteras, Aleksandra Katarzyna","Ibsen, Lars Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-762158"],"event":{"end":"2024-08-30","place":"Lisbon, pt","start":"2024-08-26","title":"ECSMGE 24","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Analytical methods","CPT based methods","Experiments","Screw piles"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prediction of uplift and compression bearing capacity of screw piles in saturated sand prévision de la capacité de charge en compression et en soulèvement des pieux vissés dans le sable saturé","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1201/9781003431749-31","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-762158","ids":["aau-2a01d191-a880-4f1c-8db1-35b5041e3071"],"keyword":["Analytical methods","CPT-based methods","Experiments","Screw piles"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-070DEDDCA6806E85B0F53DBB92E6D2E3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/762593921/Prediction_of_uplift_and_compression_bearing_capacity_of_screw_piles_in_saturated_sand_25_01_15_08_54_58.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/576779705/Prediction_of_uplift_and_compression_bearing_capacity_of_screw_piles_in_saturated_sand.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1201/9781003431749-31","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Structures, Geotechnics and Risk","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Geotechnical Engineering and Offshore Foundations Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel Kristian","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"cd6949ad-ae79-4c1f-99a9-72c2afeeed3f","name":"Andreasen, Daniel Kristian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Aleksandra Katarzyna","key":"koteraspau","last":"Koteras","locid":"a7438315-bb6a-4efa-b4d3-d48fda2ab067","name":"Koteras, Aleksandra Katarzyna","orcid":"0000-0001-5761-807X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Bo","key":"ibsenpau","last":"Ibsen","locid":"23b734a4-b2f7-44cd-ba17-e812ddc3640c","name":"Ibsen, Lars Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-1304-6660","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nuno","key":"guerrapedh","last":"Guerra","name":"Guerra, Nuno","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Manuel","key":"matosfernandespedh","last":"Matos Fernandes","name":"Matos Fernandes, Manuel","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Cristiana","key":"ferreirapedh","last":"Ferreira","name":"Ferreira, Cristiana","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"António","key":"gomescorreiapedh","last":"Gomes Correia","name":"Gomes Correia, António","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Alexandre","key":"pintopedh","last":"Pinto","name":"Pinto, Alexandre","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Pedro","key":"sêcoepintopedh","last":"Sêco e Pinto","name":"Sêco e Pinto, Pedro","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1201/9781003431749-31","edition":"1st Edition","eisbn":["9781003431749"],"isbn":["9781032548166"],"pages":"311-314","place":"London","publisher":"CRC Press","status":"p","subtitle":"PROCEEDINGS OF THE XVIII EUROPEAN CONFERENCE ON SOIL MECHANICS AND GEOTECHNICALENGINEERING","title":"Geotechnical Engineering Challenges to Meet Current and Emerging Needs of Society"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["12. Responsible Consumption and Production","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-2a01d191-a880-4f1c-8db1-35b5041e3071"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Prediction of uplift and compression bearing capacity of screw piles in saturated sand : Prévision de la capacité de charge en compression et en soulèvement des pieux vissés dans le sable saturé","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-762158","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Objective: To investigate the prevalence and experience of symptom flares in women with Chronic Pelvic Pain (CPP) as well as their triggers Design: Cross-sectional questionnaire within the Translational Research in Pelvic Pain clinical cohort study. Setting: Women with CPP, with subgroups of women with endometriosis (EAP), interstitial cystitis/bladder pain syndrome (BPS), comorbid endometriosis and interstitial cystitis/bladder pain syndrome (EABP), and those with pelvic pain without endometriosis or interstitial cystitis/bladder pain syndrome (PP). Population or sample: 100 participants across subgroups. Methods: Questionnaire within large cohort study. Main Outcome Measures: The prevalence and characteristics of short, medium and long symptom flares in CPP. Results: 76% of women with CPP experience symptom flares of at least one length (short, medium and/or long). Flares are associated with painful and non-painful symptoms. There is large variation amongst those with CPP for the frequency, duration, symptoms and triggers for these flares. Participants reported flares as stopping them from doing things they would usually do, participants thinking about symptoms of flares as well as flares being bothersome. Conclusions: Flares are prevalent and clinically very important in the context of CPP. More research is needed to elucidate the mechanisms and characteristics underlying flares. Clinical practice should include an enquiry of flares with the aim of finding strategies to lessen their burden.","author_count":24,"contributors":["Coxon, Lydia","Lugt, Celia","Horne, Andrew","Evans, Emma","Abreu-Mendes, Pedro","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","Aziz, Qasim","Becker, Christian","Birch, Judy","Charrua, Ana","Demetriou, Lysia","Ferreira-Gomes, Joana","Hoffman, Anja","Hummelshoj, Lone","Krassowski, Michal","Lunde, Claire","Meijlink, Jane","Missmer, Stacey","Perro, Danielle","Zondervan, Krina","Sieberg, Christine","Cruz, Francisco","Nagel, Jens","Vincent, Katy"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-805531"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Netherlands","Portugal","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bayer AG","Boston Children's Hospital","Centro Hospitalar Universitário de São João","Endometriosis.org","International Painful Bladder Foundation","Pelvic Pain Support Network","Queen Mary University of London","University of Edinburgh","University of Oxford"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"symptom flares a clinically important but under explored challenge for women with chronic pelvic pain","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dpr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.22541/au.172146589.95819306/v1","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funding: This project has received funding from the Innovative Medicines Initiative 2 Joint Undertaking under grant agreement No 777500. This Joint Undertaking receives support from the European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and innovation programme and EFPIA Companies."],"id":"S01-000.00-805531","ids":["aau-d2795093-45ff-4e47-a43c-e3b44f7285b8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-A47F81837CFBBC66113924D5ADB277D8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.22541/au.172146589.95819306/v1","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of oxford","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Oxford","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of edinburgh","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Un