{"abstract":"Avian traces occurring in Pleistocene aeolianite and beach deposits are rare and relatively poorly known, despite being good paleoenvironmental indicators. Passeriform and raptorial birds are especially rare in the track fossil record. Exceptional tracksites were found in the Malhão formation, a Pleistocene coastal aeolianite unit from the SW mainland Portugal, with subunits in the interval ∼187 to ∼27 ka. Two new forms of avian traces were identified, Corvidichnus odemirensis and Buboichnus vicentinus - attributed to the locomotion of Western jackdaw and the locomotion and predation/feeding behaviour of a large Eagle-owl. The last trace fossil may correspond to the first evidence of a raptorial bird-prey interaction found in action in the fossil record. Typical shorebird tracks and trackways attributed to gulls (Laridae) and curlews, and others tentatively compared with Rallidae, such as Eurasian coot, are also discussed within the aeolianite ichnoassemblages. The tracks here described are the first avian ichnotaxa from the Pleistocene of Europe.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Neto de Carvalho, Carlos","Belo, João","Figueiredo, Silvério","Cunha, Pedro P.","Muñiz, Fernando","Belaústegui, Zain","Cachão, Mário","Rodriguez-Vidal, Joaquín","Cáceres, Luis M.","Baucon, Andrea","Murray, A.S.","Buylaert, Jan Pieter","Zhang, Yilu","Ferreira, Cristiana","Toscano, António","Gómez, Paula","Ramírez, Samuel","Finlayson, Geraldine","Finlayson, Stewart","Finlayson, Clive"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-672848"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Neto de Carvalho, Carlos"],"country":["China","Gibraltar","Italy","Portugal","Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Gibraltar Museum","Henan Academy of Agricultural Sciences","Polytechnic Institute of Tomar","University of Barcelona","University of Coimbra","University of Genoa","University of Huelva","University of Huevla","University of Lisbon","University of Seville"],"keyword":["Coastal habitat","Perching bird tracks","Pleistocene","SW mainland Portugal","Shorebird tracks","Zygodactyl tracks"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"coastal raptors and raiders new bird tracks in the pleistocene of sw iberian peninsula","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85162223515","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was financed by the Câmara Municipal de Odemira, by the Centro Português de Geo-História e Pré-História, (under the project RPUECE/PAL04/2016), by the Portuguese Science Foundation (FCT) through the projects UID/MAR/04292/2020 (MARE) and LA/P/0069/2020 (ARNET)UIDB/MAR/04292/2021 (MARE — Marine and Environmental Sciences Centre/ARNET), but also a Sabbatical grant (ref. SFRH/BSAB/150395/2019) hold by PPC (Programa Operacional Capital Humano). SF is funded by the project UID/Multi/00073/2020 (Centro de Geociências, Univ. Coimbra). The work of AB has been supported by the PALEOGIANTS and CAMBIACLIMA projects (University of Genova). J- PB received funding from the European Research Council under the European Union Horizon 2020 research and innovation programme ERC-2014-StG 639904 – RELOS. This work also received institutional support from the Naturtejo, E.I.M. and the Municipality of Idanha-a-Nova. A special acknowledgment to the enthusiastic support throughout these years to our research in the area of the municipality of Odemira by the Municipal Councillor for Education Isabel Palma Raposo, and Maria Filomena Patrício, technician from the Municipality. We would like to thank to all the colleagues who have collaborated in the field campaigns, and to the Editor Professor Danielle Schreve and the anonymous reviewers for the valuable comments."],"id":"S02-100.00-672848","identifier":[{"id":"85162223515","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-fd5337d1-29a3-435a-aaaa-d964b1ec6ac3","dtu-a09799ed-a196-4cfe-8b84-4a4e948f1a91"],"keyword":["Coastal habitat","Perching bird tracks","Pleistocene","SW mainland Portugal","Shorebird tracks","Zygodactyl tracks"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-016E3C177DFA5675E41C9F2E8FD23E46"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"pt","key":"university of lisbon","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Lisbon","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"pt","key":"university of coimbra","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Coimbra","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"pt","key":"polytechnic institute of tomar","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Polytechnic Institute of Tomar","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"es","key":"university of seville","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Seville","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"es","key":"university of barcelona","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Barcelona","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"es","key":"university of huevla","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Huevla","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"es","key":"university of huelva","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Huelva","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"it","key":"university of genoa","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"nam