e":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Maria","key":"perifanoupedh","last":"Perifanou","name":"Perifanou, Maria","rank":11,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Tina","key":"papathomapedh","last":"Papathoma","name":"Papathoma, Tina","rank":12,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-42682-7_27","isbn":["9783031426810"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"399-414","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Responsive and Sustainable Educational Futures - 18th European Conference on Technology Enhanced Learning, EC-TEL 2023, Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85172010223"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-be390dd3-bdae-4b8e-9035-b29e39d0a517"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Understanding Peer Feedback Contributions Using Natural Language Processing","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-739755","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Chronic pelvic pain (CPP), despite its high prevalence, is still relatively poorly understood mechanistically. This study, as part of the Translational Research in Pelvic Pain (TRiPP) project, has used a full quantitative sensory testing (QST) paradigm to profile n = 85 women with and without CPP (endometriosis or bladder pain specifically). We used the foot as a control site and abdomen as the test site. Across 5 diagnostically determined subgroups, we found features which are common across different aetiologies, eg, gain of function in pressure pain threshold (PPT) when assessing responses from the lower abdomen or pelvis (referred pain site). However, disease-specific phenotypes were also identified, eg, greater mechanical allodynia in endometriosis, despite there being large heterogeneities within diagnostic groups. The most common QST sensory phenotype was mechanical hyperalgesia (>50% across all the groups). A \"healthy' sensory phenotype was seen in <7% of CPP participants. Specific QST measures correlated with sensory symptoms assessed by the painDETECT questionnaire (pressure-evoked pain [painDETECT] and PPT [QST] [r = 0.47, P < 0.001]; mechanical hyperalgesia (painDETECT) and mechanical pain sensitivity [MPS from QST] [r = 0.38, P = 0.009]). The data suggest that participants with CPP are sensitive to both deep tissue and cutaneous inputs, suggesting that central mechanisms may be important in this cohort. We also see phenotypes such as thermal hyperalgesia, which may be the result of peripheral mechanisms, such as irritable nociceptors. This highlights the importance of stratifying patients into clinically meaningful phenotypes, which may have implications for the development of better therapeutic strategies for CPP.","author_count":27,"contributors":["Coxon, Lydia","Vollert, Jan","Perro, Danielle","Lunde, Claire E","Ferreira-Gomes, Joana","Charrua, Ana","Abreu-Mendes, Pedro","Krassowski, Michal","Birch, Judy","Meijlink, Jane","Hummelshoj, Lone","Hoffmann, Anja","Aziz, Qasim","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","Pogatzki-Zahn, Esther","Evans, Emma","Demetriou, Lysia","McMahon, Stephen B","Missmer, Stacey A","Becker, Christian M","Zondervan, Krina T","Horne, Andrew W","Cruz, Francisco","Sieberg, Christine B","Treede, Rolf-Detlef","Nagel, Jens","Vincent, Katy"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-674103"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Coxon, Lydia"],"country":["Germany","Netherlands","Portugal","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bayer AG","Boston Children's Hospital","Centro Hospitalar Universitário de São João","Endometriosis.org","Harvard University","Heidelberg University ","Imperial College London","International Painful Bladder Foundation","King's College London","Michigan State University","Pelvic Pain Support Network","Queen Mary University of London","University Hospital Münster","University Medical Center Schleswig-Holstein","University of Edinburgh","University of Oxford","University of Porto"],"keyword":["Bladder pain syndrome","Chronic Pain diagnosis","Chronic pelvic pain","Endometriosis","Female","Humans","Hyperalgesia","Interstitial cystitis","Pain Measurement methods","Pain Threshold physiology","Pelvic Pain","Quantitative sensory testing","Translational Research Biomedical"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comprehensive quantitative sensory testing shows altered sensory function in women with chronic pelvic pain results from the translational research in pelvic pain tripp study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/j.pain.0000000000002955","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Authors thank Natalie Cuccia (for help collecting data), Miriam Szabo (for data entry), Emily Tan (for data entry), and Lewis Carney (for data entry). This project has received funding from the Innovative Medicines Initiative 2 Joint Undertaking under grant agreement No 777500. This Joint Undertaking receives support from the European Union's Horizon 2020 research and innovation programme and EFPIA Companies. This project was preregistered on clinicaltrials.gov : NCT04001244. Center for Neuroplasticity and Pain (CNAP) is supported by the Danish National Research Foundation (DNRF121). Financial support was provided by the J. Willard and Alice S. Marriott Foundation for establishment of and baseline data collection within the A2A cohort—from which the Boston-based TRiPP population was sampled."],"id":"S01-000.00-674103","identifier":[{"id":"37289573","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85174751930","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-c786c7c8-9cc8-43bc-8c27-0efbe629ceeb"],"keyword":["Bladder pain syndrome","Chronic Pain/diagnosis","Chronic pelvic pain","Endometriosis","Female","Humans","Hyperalgesia","Interstitial cystitis","Pain Measurement/methods","Pain Threshold/physiology","Pelvic Pain","Quantitative sensory testing","Translational Research, Biomedical"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FE06B02E309BFD6AAC59EE10C2CDD2A0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/j.pain.0000000000002955","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/567605360/comprehensive_quantitative_sensory_testing_shows.13.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of oxford","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Oxford","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university hospital münster","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University Hospital Münster","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"heidelberg university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Heidelberg University ","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"imperial college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Imperial College London","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"de","key":"university medical center schleswig holstein","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University Medical Center Schleswig-Holstein","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"us","key":"boston children s hospital","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Boston Children's Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"pt","key":"university of porto","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Porto","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"pt","key":"centro hospitalar universitário de são joão","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Centro Hospitalar Universitário de São João","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"gb","key":"pelvic pain support network","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Pelvic Pain Support Network","used":1},{"affno":"10","country":"nl","key":"international painful bladder foundation","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"International Painful Bladder Foundation","used":1},{"affno":"11","country":"gb","key":"endometriosis org","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Endometriosis.org","used":1},{"affno":"12","country":"de","key":"bayer ag","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Bayer AG","used":1},{"affno":"13","country":"gb","key":"queen mary university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Queen Mary University of London","used":1},{"affno":"14","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nor