ty"],"title":"Comprehensive quantitative sensory testing shows altered sensory function in women with chronic pelvic pain : results from the Translational Research in Pelvic Pain (TRiPP) Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-674103","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Although analog-to-digital converters (ADCs) are critical components in mixed-signal integrated circuits (IC), their performance has not been improved significantly over the last decade. To achieve a radical improvement (compact, low power and reliable ADCs), spintronics can be considered as a proper candidate due to its compatibility with CMOS and wide applications in storage, neuromorphic computing, and so on. In this paper, a proof-of-concept of a 3-bit spin-CMOS Flash ADC using in-plane-anisotropy magnetic tunnel junctions (i-MTJs) with spin-orbit torque (SOT) switching mechanism is designed, fabricated and characterized. In this ADC, each MTJ plays the role of a comparator whose threshold is set by the engineering of the heavy metal (HM) width. Such an approach can reduce the ADC footprint. Monte-Carlo simulations based on the experimental measurements show the process variations/mismatch limits the accuracy of the proposed ADC to 2 bits. Moreover, the maximum differential nonlinearity (DNL) and integral nonlinearity (INL) are 0.739 LSB (least significant bit) and 0.7319 LSB, respectively.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Ghanatian, Hamdam","Benetti, Luana","Anacleto, Pedro","Böhnert, Tim","Farkhani, Hooman","Ferreira, Ricardo","Moradi, Farshad"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-675091"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Portugal"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","International Iberian Nanotechnology Laboratory"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"spin orbit torque flash analog to digital converter","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-023-35845-7","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-675091","identifier":[{"id":"85161655587","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10256753","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37296130","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-6a4c4c7e-bd2b-4d7b-a551-ed56162af998"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B8AB905B03A13FBF0CF9B9BCC5196AAA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-023-35845-7","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"pt","key":"international iberian nanotechnology laboratory","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"International Iberian Nanotechnology Laboratory","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering - Electronics and Photonics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Hamdam","key":"ghanatianpau","last":"Ghanatian","name":"Ghanatian, Hamdam","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luana","key":"benettipau","last":"Benetti","name":"Benetti, Luana","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro","key":"anacletopau","last":"Anacleto","name":"Anacleto, Pedro","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tim","key":"böhnertpau","last":"Böhnert","name":"Böhnert, Tim","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hooman","key":"farkhanipau","last":"Farkhani","locid":"035de3d4-136b-49e3-8011-f2ef86685a3f","name":"Farkhani, Hooman","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ricardo","key":"ferreirapau","last":"Ferreira","name":"Ferreira, Ricardo","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Farshad","key":"moradipau","last":"Moradi","locid":"3992dea8-cf6f-44c7-b1b9-26927a42aab7","name":"Moradi, Farshad","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37296130"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-023-35845-7","issn":["20452322"],"issue":"1","journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"9416","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85161655587"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6a4c4c7e-bd2b-4d7b-a551-ed56162af998"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Spin-orbit torque flash analog-to-digital converter","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-675091","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Aims: Multimorbidity, the coexistence of two or more chronic conditions, is synonymous with heart failure (HF). How risk related to comorbidities compares at individual and population levels is unknown. The aim of this study is to examine the risk related to comorbidities, alone and in combination, both at individual and population levels. Methods and results: Using two clinical trials in HF – the Prospective comparison of ARNI (Angiotensin Receptor–Neprilysin Inhibitor) with ACEI (Angiotensin-Converting Enzyme Inhibitor) to Determine Impact on Global Mortality and morbidity in HF trial (PARADIGM-HF) and the Aliskiren Trial to Minimize Outcomes in Patients with Heart Failure trials (ATMOSPHERE) – we identified the 10 most common comorbidities and examined 45 possible pairs. We calculated population attributable fractions (PAF) for all-cause death and relative excess risk due to interaction with Cox proportional hazard models. Of 15 066 patients in the study, 14 133 (93.7%) had at least one and 11 867 (78.8%) had at least two of the 10 most prevalent comorbidities. The greatest individual risk among pairs was associated with peripheral artery disease (PAD) in combination with stroke (hazard ratio [HR] 1.73; 95% confidence interval [CI] 1.28–2.33) and anaemia (HR 1.71; 95% CI 1.39–2.11). The combination of chronic kidney disease (CKD) and hypertension had the highest PAF (5.65%; 95% CI 3.66–7.61). Two pairs demonstrated significant synergistic interaction (atrial fibrillation with CKD and coronary artery disease, respectively) and one an antagonistic interaction (anaemia and obesity). Conclusions: In HF, the impact of multimorbidity differed at the individual patient and population level, depending on the prevalence of and the risk related to each comorbidity, and the interaction between individual comorbidities. Patients with coexistent PAD and stroke were at greatest individual risk whereas, from a population perspective, coexistent CKD and hypertension mattered most.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Dewan, Pooja","Ferreira, João Pedro","Butt, Jawad H.","Petrie, Mark C.","Abraham, William T.","Desai, Akshay S.","Dickstein, Kenneth","Køber, Lars","Packer, Milton","Rouleau, Jean L.","Stewart, Simon","Swedberg, Karl","Zile, Michael R.","Solomon, Scott D.","Jhund, Pardeep S.","McMurray, John J.V."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-684225"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Canada","Norway","Portugal","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Baylor University Medical Center at Dallas","Harvard University","Medical University of South Carolina","Ohio State University","University of Bergen","University of Glasgow","University of Gothenburg","University of Montreal","University of Notre Dame Australia","University of Porto"],"keyword":["Heart failure with reduced ejection fraction","Multimorbidity"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact of multimorbidity on mortality in heart failure with reduced ejection fraction which comorbidities matter most an analysis of paradigm hf and atmosphere","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/360030680/IKM_European_J_of_Heart_Fail_2023_Dewan_Impact_of_multimorbidity_on_mortality_in_HFrEF_Which_comorbidities_matter_most.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-684225","identifier":[{"id":"37062869","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85153605636","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-8ba87efc-bd62-4196-b5ac-4cd7e0dd25d3"],"keyword":["Heart failure with reduced ejection fraction","Multimorbidity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-81A32620A2EDEE5F65144CE685DB5712"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/360030680/IKM_European_J_of_Heart_Fail_2023_Dewan_Impact_of_multimorbidity_on_mortality_in_HFrEF_Which_comorbidities_matter_most.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of glasgow","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Glasgow","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"pt","key":"university of porto","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Porto","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"ohio state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Ohio State University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"harvard university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Harvard University","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"no","key":"university of bergen","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Bergen","used":1},{"affno":"7","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medi