{"abstract":"There are significant sex differences in the clinical characteristics of cocaine use disorder (CUD). As this is a brain disorder that involves changes in functional connectivity, we investigated the existence of sex differences among people with CUD and controls. We used a data-driven method comparing males (n = 20, CK-M) and females with CUD (n = 20, CK-F) and healthy controls (20 males, HC-M and 20 females, HC-F). The participants undertook a resting-state functional magnetic resonance imaging exam. Regional homogeneity (ReHo) was performed to identify group and sex differences. Persons with CUD of both sexes presented lower ReHo parameters than controls, especially within the parietal lobule. Males with CUD showed higher ReHo than females in three right-side brain areas: postcentral gyrus, putamen and fusiform gyrus. It was found that abstinence symptoms severity was associated with lower ReHo values in the right postcentral gyrus and the right fusiform gyrus. Participants with CUD exhibited altered ReHo parameters compared to controls, similar to what is found in ageing-related disorders. Our data also indicate that cocaine has sex-specific effects on brain functioning when analysing ReHo.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Sanvicente-Vieira, Breno","Rothmann, Leonardo Melo","Esper, Nathalia Bianchini","Tondo, Lucca Pizzato","Ferreira, Pedro Eugênio","Buchweitz, Augusto","Franco, Alexandre Rosa","Grassi-Oliveira, Rodrigo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-144395"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","America, South","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Grassi-Oliveira, Rodrigo"],"country":["Brazil","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Child Mind Institute, Inc.","Nathan S. Kline Institute for Psychiatric Research","New York University","Pontificia Universidade Catolica do Rio Grande do Sul","Pontificia Universidade Catolica do Rio de Janeiro","University of Connecticut"],"keyword":["Resting state"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sex differences in brain regional homogeneity during acute abstinence in cocaine use disorder","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/adb.13177","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-144395","identifier":[{"id":"85128807211","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9285589","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35470550","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-1a45bc30-a0c8-46e8-9c7f-ad1e9cf58807"],"keyword":["cocaine sex differences","resting-state","substance use and related disorders"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B8A2EFA3EBD2E6A4699CB14330459801"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9285589/pdf/ADB-27-0.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/adb.13177","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"br","key":"pontificia universidade catolica do rio grande do sul","loc":["Brazil","America, South"],"name":"Pontificia Universidade Catolica do Rio Grande do Sul","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"br","key":"pontificia universidade catolica do rio de janeiro","loc":["Brazil","America, South"],"name":"Pontificia Universidade Catolica do Rio de Janeiro","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of connecticut","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Connecticut","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"nathan s kline institute for psychiatric research","loc":["United 