{"abstract":"O objetivo desse trabalho foi verificar e comparar as características microarquiteturais do tecido ósseo peri-implantar de ratos obesos e não obesos por meio de microtomografia computadorizada (micro CT). Para isso, 20 ratos Wistar machos foram divididos em dois grupos, obesos (GO) e não obesos (GNO). Inicialmente, o GO foi submetido a dieta hiperlipídica complementada com dieta de cafeteria por 90 dias para o estabelecimento da obesidade enquanto o GNO recebeu dieta padrão. Em seguida, foram instalados implantes osseintegráveis na tíbia de todos os animais. A eutanásia foi feita após 60 dias e as tíbias seguiram para a análise tridimensional por micro CT na qual foram avaliados parâmetros que caracterizam o trabeculado ósseo, como espessura do trabeculado ósseo (Tb.th), número (Tb.N) e separação (Tb.S) das trabéculas óssea, porosidade óssea (Po(tot)), superfície de intersecção óssea (iS), volume de densidade óssea (Bv. Tv) e densidade de conectividade (Conn.Dn). Os dados foram submetidos a teste estatístico com nível de significância de 95%. Diferenças significantes foram observadas na Tb.S, sendo maior no GO (0,1348mm) em comparação ao GNO (0,1263mm); e na Conn.Dn, que obteve valores maiores no GNO (1/207mm3) do que no GO (768,3mm3). Conclui-se que o tecido ósseo peri-implantar dos ratos obesos, mostrando maior separação e menor conectividade entre as trabéculas, pode sugerir um tecido ósseo de maior fragilidade.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Cândido, Lauriene Regina","de Souza Batista, Fabio Roberto","Gomes Ferreira, Pedro Henrique Silva","Manzolli Leite, Fabio Renato","Nascimento, Gustavo G.","Pinto Farias, Paulo Esteves","Okamoto, Roberta","Furuse, Cristiane"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-263312"],"event":{"end":"2020-09-12","place":"Online, br","start":"2020-09-09","title":"37th Annual Meeting of the Brazilian division of the International Academy of Dental Research","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, South"],"corresponding_author":["Furuse, Cristiane"],"country":["Brazil"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","São Paulo State University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"influência da obesidade na microarquitetura do tecido ósseo periimplantar estudo em ratos","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://sbpqo.org.br/hotsite2020/anais.asp","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-263312","ids":["au-eabb527a-7fa7-455d-97fb-8efa560ebbe2"],"lang":"Portuguese","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-EA7A47F9B8AAEB3ED757A7DC752E4412"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://sbpqo.org.br/hotsite2020/anais.asp","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"br","key":"são paulo state university","loc":["Brazil","America, South"],"name":"São Paulo State University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health - Section for Periodontology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lauriene Regina","key":"cândidopau","last":"Cândido","name":"Cândido, Lauriene Regina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabio Roberto","key":"desouzabatistapau","last":"de Souza Batista","name":"de Souza Batista, Fabio Roberto","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro Henrique Silva","key":"gomesferreirapau","last":"Gomes Ferreira","name":"Gomes Ferreira, Pedro Henrique Silva","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabio Renato","key":"manzollileitepau","last":"Manzolli Leite","locid":"7c762311-bbde-4398-9470-23e8c4de7f7c","name":"Manzolli Leite, Fabio Renato","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Gustavo G.","key":"nascimentopau","last":"Nascimento","locid":"a53794d3-0837-4938-9eb6-57ecd94767e3","name":"Nascimento, Gustavo G.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paulo Esteves","key":"pintofariaspau","last":"Pinto Farias","name":"Pinto Farias, Paulo Esteves","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Roberta","key":"okamotopau","last":"Okamoto","name":"Okamoto, Roberta","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cristiane","key":"furusepau","last":"Furuse","name":"Furuse, Cristiane","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-eabb527a-7fa7-455d-97fb-8efa560ebbe2"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Influência da obesidade na microarquitetura do tecido ósseo periimplantar - estudo em ratos","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-263312","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The aim was to provide global experts ranking on priorities in diagnostic tools for VAP in clinical practice. A multiple criteria decision analysis (MCDA) was performed to identify diagnosis tools for VAP diagnosis. Priority factors were identified after literature review. An international, multidisciplinary expert panel reviewed variables and ranked diagnostic tools. Experts from ten European hospitals participated. Regarding bedside clinical practices, seven required chest X-ray use in all patients, whereas six reported the use of blood cultures and endotracheal aspirate in all patients. Invasive techniques were routinely performed in seven sites. CRP, PCT, and Gram stains were performed in all patients by 5, 2, and 8, respectively. Impact on patient outcomes, safety, and impact on the decision to start antibiotic therapy were ranked as the top three relevant concerns (7.7/10, 7/10, and 6.9/10, respectively). Chest X-ray was ranked as the most important imaging technique to diagnose VAP (score 251.7). Apart from blood cultures, endotracheal aspirate culture was identified as the main collection method for the microbiological testing (scores of 274.8 and 246.8, respectively). Mini-BAL was the preferred invasive technique with a score of 208. Top three biomarkers were CRP (score 184.3), PCT (181.3), and WBC (166.4). Gram stain (192.5) was prioritized among laboratory diagnostic techniques. Using MCDA, it is recommended to perform a combination of diagnostic techniques including images (chest X-ray), culture of clinical specimens (blood cultures and endotracheal aspirate), and biomarkers (CRP or PCT) for VAP diagnosis at the bedside. Gram stain was ranked as the preferred laboratory technique.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Ferreira-Coimbra, João","Ardanuy, Carmen","Diaz, Emili","Leone, Marc","De Pascale, Gennaro","Póvoa, Pedro","Prat-Aymerich, Cristina","Serrano-Garcia, Ricardo","Solé-Violan, Jordi","Zaragoza, Rafael","Rello, Jordi"],"cuid":["S01-0