{"abstract":"Collecting complex information on the status of machinery is the enabler for advanced maintenance activities, and one of the main players in this process is the sensor. This paper describes modern maintenance strategies that lead to Condition-Based Maintenance. This paper discusses the sensors that can be used to support maintenance, as of different categories, spanning from common off-the-shelf sensors, to specialized sensors monitoring very specific characteristics, and to virtual sensors. This paper also presents four different real-world examples of project pilots that make use of the described sensors and draws a comparison between them. In particular, each scenario has unique characteristics requiring different families of sensors, but on the other hand provides similar characteristics on other aspects.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Albano, Michele","Ferreira, Luis","Di Orio, Giovanni","Maló, Pedro","Webers, Godfried","Jantunen, Erkki","Gabilondo, Iosu","Viguera, Mikel","Papa, Gregor"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-100594"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Albano, Michele"],"country":["Finland","Netherlands","Portugal","Slovenia","Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","IK4-Ikerlan Technology Research Centre","Institute of Engineering of Porto","J. Stefan Institute","Koniker","Koninklijke Philips N.V.","NOVA University Lisbon","VTT Technical Research Centre of Finland Ltd."],"keyword":["Condition based maintenance","Demonstrators","Predictive maintenance","Use cases","Virtual sensors"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"advanced sensor based maintenance in real world exemplary cases","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/00051144.2020.1794192","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was partially supported by National Funds through FCT/MEC (Portuguese Foundation for Science and Technology), Slovenian Research Agency (research core funding No. P2-0098), Finnish Funding Agency for Innovation Tekes, and co-financed by ERDF (European Regional Development Fund) under the PT2020 Partnership, within the CISTER Research Unit (CEC/04234); also by FCT/MEC and the EU ECSEL JU under the H2020 Framework Programme, within project ECSEL/0004/2014, JU grant no. 662189 (MANTIS); also by EU ECSEL JU under the H2020 Framework Programme, JU grant no. 737459 (Productive4.0 project)."],"id":"S01-000.00-100594","identifier":[{"id":"85088286774","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-ae37bda0-9604-43fb-b92d-99573b457806"],"keyword":["Condition-based maintenance","demonstrators","pilots","predictive maintenance","use cases","virtual sensors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F6A8518A2EF930F8C7C673DCEF91D27D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/00051144.2020.1794192","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/386901264/Advanced_sensor_based_maintenance_in_real_world_exemplary_cases.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department