{"abstract":"Mobility has long been a central concern in research within the Computer-Supported Cooperative Work (CSCW) community, particularly when it comes to work and how being on the move calls for reorganizing work practices. We expand this line of work with a focus on nomadic leisure practices. Based on interviews with eleven participants, we present a study that illuminates how digital technologies are used to shape and structure long-distance cycling. Our main analysis centers on bike touring as a nomadic leisure practice and on how it offers a radical departure from traditional modes of structuring work and life, and thus, complicates the relationship between work and leisure. We complement this with an account of managing the uncertainties of nomadicity by focusing on participants’ experiences with arranging overnighting and network hospitality. We offer this study, firstly, as one response to the call for more diversity in the empirical cases drawn upon in theorizing nomadic work and leisure practices, but more productively, as an opportunity to reflect upon the temporal and spatial logics of digital technologies and platforms and how they frame our attitudes towards the interplay between work and leisure.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Ferreira, Pedro","Helms, Karey","Brown, Barry","Lampinen, Airi"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384670"],"event":{"acronym":"HCI","title":"Human-Computer Interaction International Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","KTH Royal Institute of Technology","Stockholm University"],"keyword":["Bike Touring","Digital Technologies in Leisure","Mobility","Nomadic Leisure Practices","Work Leisure Relationship"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"from nomadic work to nomadic leisure practice a study of long term bike touring","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84751425/CSCW_2019_Nomadic_leisure_practice_cam_ready.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384670","identifier":[{"id":"85075087505","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e6f1a9bc-2fa0-49a0-8d46-e6f788610fa7"],"keyword":["Bike Touring","Digital Technologies in Leisure","Mobility","Nomadic Leisure Practices","Work-Leisure Relationship"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-6-482000D50CB15CA19B093E8E7A0AF21E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84751425/CSCW_2019_Nomadic_leisure_practice_cam_ready.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"stockholm university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Stockholm University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro","key":"ferreirapau","last":"Ferreira","locid":"1b3cff7f-1549-4998-b52e-0ba9093e1d01","name":"Ferreira, Pedro","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Karey","key":"helmspau","last":"Helms","name":"Helms, Karey","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Barry","key":"brownpau","last":"Brown","name":"Brown, Barry","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Airi","key":"lampinenpau","last":"Lampinen","name":"Lampinen, Airi","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3359213","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"Volume 3 Issue CSCW, November 2019","title":"Proceedings of the ACM on Human-Computer Interaction"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85075087505"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e6f1a9bc-2fa0-49a0-8d46-e6f788610fa7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"From Nomadic Work to Nomadic Leisure Practice: A study of long-term bike touring","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384670","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"In a rapidly changing world, maintenance of the good health of the marine environment requires a detailed understanding of its mechanisms of change, and the ability to detect early signals of a shift away from the equilibrium state that we assume characterized it before there was any significant human impact. Given that instrumental measurements of the oceans go back no further than a few decades, the only way in which we can assess the long-term baseline variability that characterizes the pre-perturbation equilibrium state of the marine environment is by the use of proxy records contained in stratified or layered natural archives such as corals, fish otoliths and bivalve mollusc shells.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Butler, Paul G.","Freitas, Pedro S.","Burchell, Meghan","Chauvaud, Laurent"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-310185"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Canada","France","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Memorial University of Newfoundland","The European Institute for Marine Studies","University of Exeter"],"keyword":["Archaeology","Ecosystems","Environmental Monitoring","Mollusc"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"archaeology and sclerochronology of marine bivalves","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-96776-9_21","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-310185","identifier":[{"id":"85063771748","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-129e82af-516c-41f9-a813-9419e419c318"],"keyword":["Archaeology","Ecosystems","Environmental monitoring","Marine climate","Mollusc"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E10C9BA64623891AFBB324495A8493A2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/161976931/filestore_5_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-96776-9_21","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of exeter","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Exeter","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources","Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources, Danish Shellfish Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ca","key":"memorial university of newfoundland","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Memorial University of Newfoundland","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"fr","key":"the european institute for marine studies","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"The European Institute for Marine Studies","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paul G.","key":"butlerpau","last":"Butler","name":"Butler, Paul G.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pedro Seabra","key":"freitaspau","last":"Freitas","locid":"92ce76ea-81e7-40da-aace-b50a13a5ab3d","name":"Freitas, Pedro S.","name_org":"Freitas, Pedro Seabra","orcid":"0000-0001-6900-5764","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Meghan","key":"burchellpau","last":"Burchell","name":"Burchell, Meghan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurent","key":"chauvaudpau","last":"Chauvaud","name":"Chauvaud, Laurent","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Aad C.","key":"smaalpedh","last":"Smaal","name":"Smaal, Aad C.","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Joao G.","key":"ferreirapedh","last":"Ferreira","name":"Ferreira, Joao G.","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jon","key":"grantpedh","last":"Grant","name":"Grant, Jon","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens K.","key":"petersenpedh","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Jens K.","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Øivind","key":"strandpedh","last":"Strand","name":"Strand, Øivind","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-96776-9_21","eisbn":["9783319967769"],"isbn":["9783319967752"],"pages":"413-444","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Goods and Services of Marine Bivalves"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85063771748"],"sdg":["14. Life Below Water","3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-129e82af-516c-41f9-a813-9419e419c318"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Archaeology and sclerochronology of marine bivalves","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-310185","year":"2019","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Objective: The authors aim to perform a thorough translation with cultural adaptation of the patient reported outcome tool, Low Anterior Resection Syndrome (LARS) Score, to the Portuguese language (LARS-PT) in the Portuguese population with rectal cancer, after proctectomy with anastomosis. Methods: According to the current international recommendations, we designed this study encompassing three main phases: (i) cultural and linguistic validation to European Portuguese; (ii) feasibility and reliability tests of the version obtained in the previous phase; and (iii) validity tests to produce a final version. The questionnaire was completed by 154 patients from six Portuguese Colorectal Cancer Units, and 58 completed it twice. Results: Portuguese version of LARS score showed high construct validity. Regarding the test-retest, the global Intraclass Correlation showed very strong test-retest reliability. Looking at all five items, only items 3 and 5 present a moderate correlation. LARS score was able to discriminate symptoms showing worse quality of life, in patients submitted to preoperative radio and chemotherapy. Conclusions: LARS questionnaire has been properly translated into European Portuguese, demonstrating high construct validity and reliability. This is a precise, reproducible, simple, clear and user-friendly tool for evaluating bowel function in rectal cancer patients after sphincter saving operation.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Rama, Nuno Jose","Ferreira, Pedro Lopes","Pimentel, João","Juul, Therese"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-250234"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corpau":["Portuguese PT LARS Collaborative Group"],"country":["Portugal"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Centro Hospitalar de Coimbra","University of Coimbra","University of Porto"],"keyword":["Bowel dysfunction","Quality of Life","Rectal Neoplasms","Validation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"validation of the portuguese version of the low anterior resection syndrome score","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85054153257","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-250234","identifier":[{"id":"85054153257","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-d3b99f84-6567-491c-b87e-1081f820517b"],"keyword":["Bowel dysfunction","Low anterior resection syndrome score","Quality of life","Rectal neoplasms","Validation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-95F87A3434F90856B3A39E1FA25166D8"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"pt","key":"university of porto","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Porto","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"pt","key":"university of coimbra","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Coimbra","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"pt","key":"centro hospitalar de coimbra","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Centro Hospitalar de Coimbra","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Surgical Gastroenterology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":6,"key":"portuguese pt lars collaborative group","name":"Portuguese PT LARS Collaborative Group","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nuno Jose","key":"ramapau","last":"Rama","name":"Rama, Nuno Jose","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro Lopes","key":"ferreirapau","last":"Ferreira","name":"Ferreira, Pedro Lopes","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"João","key":"pimentelpau","last":"Pimentel","name":"Pimentel, João","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Therese","key":"juulpau","last":"Juul","locid":"350edc19-7579-4439-abe4-2c8a8a03ef8e","name":"Juul, Therese","orcid":"0000-0002-5411-4826","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jcol.2018.09.004","issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Coloproctology","pages":"1-8","status":"p","title":"Journal of Coloproctology","volume":"39"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85054153257"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d3b99f84-6567-491c-b87e-1081f820517b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Validation of the Portuguese version of the low anterior resection syndrome score","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-250234","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: This study aimed to evaluate the effects of radiotherapy on biomechanical, histomorphometric, and microstructural characteristics of bone, in diverse periods, compared with intact bone tissue. MATERIALS AND METHODS: Eighteen adult male New Zealand rabbits were treated with a single radiation dose of 30 Gy. The animals were randomly divided into six groups: NoIr, control group, no radiation, and five irradiated groups sacrificed after 24 h (Ir24h), 7 (Ir7d), 14 (Ir14d), 21 (Ir21d), and 28 (Ir28d) days. After these periods, the animals were sacrificed and their tibias (n = 6) evaluated using three-point bending test to calculate the ultimate force, work to failure, and bone stiffness. Dynamic indentation test was used to quantify Vickers hardness and elasticity modulus of bone tissue. Micro-CT was used to analyze the cortical volume (CtV), cortical thickness (CtTh), and porosity (Ct.Po). Histomorphometric assessment was based on the lacunarity of bone tissue. Data were analyzed using one-way ANOVA and Kruskal-Wallis tests followed by Tukey, Dunnet, and Dunn's post-tests (P < 0.05). RESULTS: The ultimate force, work to failure, stiffness, elastic modulus, and Vickers hardness values of irradiated bone were significantly lower that non-irradiated bone. Irradiated bone showed significantly lower CtTh and CtV values and higher CtPo than non-irradiated bone. No significant difference was found for lacunarity between non-irradiated bone and irradiated bone. CONCLUSIONS: Ionizing radiation decreases normal anisotropy on microarchitecture of cortical bone, and increases bone fragility compared with non-irradiated bone. Further, these changes were seen after longer periods (e.g., 14 and 21 days), and not immediately after radiation therapy. CLINICAL RELEVANCE: The radiotherapy reduces bone mechanical properties and the normal structure of organic and inorganic bone matrix. For studying the protocols to protect the radiotherapy effect using rabbit model, the use of the sacrificing period between 14 and 21 days is recommended.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Soares, Priscilla Barbosa Ferreira","Soares, Carlos José","Limirio, Pedro Henrique Justino Oliveira","de Jesus, Rainde Naiara Rezende","Dechichi, Paula","Spin-Neto, Rubens","Zanetta-Barbosa, Darceny"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-273686"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, South"],"country":["Brazil"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Universidade Federal de Uberlandia"],"keyword":["Biomechanics","Bone","Cortical bone","Creep","Dental Implants","Ionizing radiation","Microcomputed tomography","Mineralization","Nanoindentation","Osteoradionecrosis","Radiotherapy","Strength","TISSUE","X ray irradiation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of ionizing radiation after therapy interval on bone histomorphometric and biomechanical characteristics","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85055719098","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-273686","identifier":[{"id":"85055719098","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000467444800024","type":"wos"},{"id":"30368663","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-fd0a177b-ec37-432f-84f5-b9a413a8f463"],"keyword":["Biomechanics","Bone","CORTICAL BONE","CREEP","DENTAL IMPLANTS","Ionizing radiation","MINERALIZATION","Microcomputed tomography","NANOINDENTATION","OSTEORADIONECROSIS","RADIOTHERAPY","STRENGTH","TISSUE","X-RAY-IRRADIATION"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EE5FBA5F45D84098089E035ABBE34078"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"br","key":"universidade federal de uberlandia","loc":["Brazil","America, South"],"name":"Universidade Federal de Uberlandia","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health - Section for Oral Radiology and Endodontics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Priscilla Barbosa Ferreira","key":"soarespriscillabarbosaferreirapau","last":"Soares","name":"Soares, Priscilla Barbosa Ferreira","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carlos José","key":"soarescarlosjosépau","last":"Soares","name":"Soares, Carlos José","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro Henrique Justino Oliveira","key":"limiriopedrohenriquejustinooliveirapau","last":"Limirio","name":"Limirio, Pedro Henrique Justino Oliveira","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rainde Naiara Rezende","key":"dejesusraindenaiararezendepau","last":"de Jesus","name":"de Jesus, Rainde Naiara Rezende","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paula","key":"dechichipaulapau","last":"Dechichi","name":"Dechichi, Paula","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rubens","key":"spinnetorubenspau","last":"Spin-Neto","locid":"242a9551-55e4-4564-afdd-f51a3ad8947b","name":"Spin-Neto, Rubens","orcid":"0000-0002-9562-0610","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Darceny","key":"zanettabarbosadarcenypau","last":"Zanetta-Barbosa","name":"Zanetta-Barbosa, Darceny","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30368663"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00784-018-2724-3","issn":["14326981","14363771"],"issn_org":["14326981"],"issue":"6","journal":"Clinical Oral Investigations","pages":"2785-2793","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Clinical Oral Investigations","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85055719098"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-fd0a177b-ec37-432f-84f5-b9a413a8f463"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Effect of ionizing radiation after-therapy interval on bone: : histomorphometric and biomechanical characteristics","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-273686","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Enjoyment has a difficult place in academia where it rarely features in its own right, as an intrinsically worthwhile pursuit. In this work we are interested in a particular form of enjoyment: holiday making, or traveling for enjoyment. In technology, this features more prominently in terms of transportation (e.g. planes, cars, booking websites) or recommender systems (e.g. tripadvisor, yelp). Our work focuses on long term, long distance, cycling, which defies traditional rationales of holiday mentality, involving exertion, exhaustion, surrendering to the elements, to the moment, and temporalities. It is about “escaping the world of interiors” to quote Rebecca Solnit, challenging 'yelp mentality'. We conducted a study of long term cyclists interviewed before and after their journeys. The interviews were focused on motivations and experiences, as well as on technological and infrastructural aspects. Amongst many aspects, participants reflected on the particular tradeoffs between pace and efficiency particular to these experiences, the attention to infrastructural constraints and opportunities as well as on the use of digital technologies. This problematises self-tracking technologies, often anchored in ideals of efficiency and performance, while simultaneously engaging in the kinds of bodily activities that these technologies are built for. This work adds to our understanding on the role that technology has in enjoyment, and particularly, holiday making. We reconsider enjoyment through the lenses of bodily exertion, the inescapable steadiness of pace, repair work and scarcity of choice and infrastructure.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Ferreira, Pedro"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381406"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Academic Enjoyment","Digital Tourism","Infrastructural Constraints","Long Distance Cycling","Self tracking Technologies"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exertion and escaping the holiday rationale","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-381406","ids":["itu-0a20a9f5-6e9f-4cf7-91ee-47bfddc6b5b6"],"keyword":["Academic Enjoyment","Digital Tourism","Infrastructural Constraints","Long Distance Cycling","Self-tracking Technologies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C86F25C6592C3F469EA041E36B3CD69D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro","key":"ferreirapau","last":"Ferreira","locid":"1b3cff7f-1549-4998-b52e-0ba9093e1d01","name":"Ferreira, Pedro","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0a20a9f5-6e9f-4cf7-91ee-47bfddc6b5b6"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Exertion and Escaping the Holiday Rationale","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381406","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"We present a study of long-term outdoor activities, based on altogether 34 interviews with 19 participants. Our goal was not only to explore these enjoyable experiences, but more broadly to examine how technology use was recontextualized ‘away’ from the everyday. Outdoor activities are commonly presented as an escape from our technology-infused world. In contrast, our interviews reveal experiences that are heavily dependent on technology, both digital and not. However, digital technology — and in particular the mobile phone — is reconfigured when taken out of its ordinary, often urban and indoor, context. We first present a diversity of ‘aways’ during outdoor activities by depicting cherished freedoms and interpersonal preferences. We then describe how participants managed connection and disconnection while away and upon coming back. To conclude, we discuss how constructions of away can support more purposeful engagements with digital technology, and how pointed (dis)connection can be useful for technology design also in non-outdoor settings.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Helms, Karey","Ferreira, Pedro","Brown, Barry","Lampinen, Airi"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382045"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","KTH Royal Institute of Technology","Stockholm University"],"keyword":["Digital dependency","Long term outdoor activities","Managed dis connection","Mobile phone usage","Technology recontextualization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"away and dis connection reconsidering the use of digital technologies in light of long term outdoor activities","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3361111","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382045","identifier":[{"id":"85076702254","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-34e8240f-a34f-4475-ae6a-f2dc63a3d9e4"],"keyword":["Digital dependency","Long-term outdoor activities","Managed (dis)connection","Mobile phone usage","Technology recontextualization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CCBB438CEA7B71F68F5474E8D1AF2881"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84739530/group230_helms.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3361111","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"stockholm university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Stockholm University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karey","key":"helmspau","last":"Helms","name":"Helms, Karey","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro","key":"ferreirapau","last":"Ferreira","locid":"1b3cff7f-1549-4998-b52e-0ba9093e1d01","name":"Ferreira, Pedro","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Barry","key":"brownpau","last":"Brown","name":"Brown, Barry","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Airi","key":"lampinenpau","last":"Lampinen","name":"Lampinen, Airi","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3361111","issn":["03624021","15733386"],"issn_org":["03624021"],"journal":"Group","paperid":"230","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Group","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85076702254"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-34e8240f-a34f-4475-ae6a-f2dc63a3d9e4"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Away and (Dis)connection: Reconsidering the Use of Digital Technologies in Light of Long-Term Outdoor Activities","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382045","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"This paper discusses researcher marginalization based on three individual vignettes, drawn out from personal experiences. The goal is to extend discussions of marginalization of research to the researchers themselves, how they are othered [5] and how we can draw on methods to address these issues. We discuss implications and ways forward, namely (1) the kinds of data we can/should collect, (2) organizing inclusive conferences and (3) how to start a wider dialogue without furthering the othering of these researchers.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Ferreira, Pedro"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383092"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Dialogue in Academia","Inclusive Conferences","Inclusive Research Practices","Researcher Marginalization","Researcher Othering"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"researchers at the margins othering and community solidarity","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://cscwsolidarity.files.wordpress.com/2018/10/pedro_ferreira_cscw_solidarity_2018.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383092","ids":["itu-7bfb875e-3dd1-47d1-9edd-076dd4935849"],"keyword":["Dialogue in Academia","Inclusive Conferences","Inclusive Research Practices","Researcher Marginalization","Researcher Othering"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8B422EB328C45A0A7D75A1F94275A449"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://cscwsolidarity.files.wordpress.com/2018/10/pedro_ferreira_cscw_solidarity_2018.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro","key":"ferreirapau","last":"Ferreira","locid":"1b3cff7f-1549-4998-b52e-0ba9093e1d01","name":"Ferreira, Pedro","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7bfb875e-3dd1-47d1-9edd-076dd4935849"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Researchers at the Margins : Othering and Community Solidarity","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383092","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"In light of recent alarming trends in human population growth, climate change, and other environmental modifications, a “Warning to humanity” manifesto was published in BioScience in 2017. This call reiterated most of the ideas originally expressed by the Union of Concerned Scientists in 1992, including the fear that we are “pushing Earth's ecosystems beyond their capacities to support the web of life.” As subterranean biologists, we take this opportunity to emphasize the global importance and the conservation challenges associated with subterranean ecosystems. They likely represent the most widespread nonmarine environments on Earth, but specialized subterranean organisms remain among the least documented and studied. Largely overlooked in conservation policies, subterranean habitats play a critical role in the function of the web of life and provide important ecosystem services. We highlight the main threats to subterranean ecosystems and propose a set of effective actions to protect this globally important natural heritage.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Mammola, Stefano","Cardoso, Pedro","Culver, David C","Deharveng, Louis","Ferreira, Rodrigo L","Fišer, Cene","Galassi, Diana M P","Griebler, Christian","Halse, Stuart","Humphreys, William F","Isaia, Marco","Malard, Florian","Martinez, Alejandro","Moldovan, Oana T","Niemiller, Matthew L","Pavlek, Martina","Reboleira, Ana Sofia","Souza-silva, Marconi","Teeling, Emma C","Wynne, J Judson","Zagmajster, Maja"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-523942"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"scientists warning on the conservation of subterranean ecosystems","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/255682270/Scientists_warning_on_the_conservation_of_subterranean_ecosystems_Author_Manuscript_.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-523942","identifier":[{"id":"85070471050","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-da8342a5-a59f-4318-9a3b-20ff2aeeb5bc"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-F821CCD5781346B7DD759FAA7C72F114"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/255682270/Scientists_warning_on_the_conservation_of_subterranean_ecosystems_Author_Manuscript_.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, The Natural History Museum, Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Stefano","key":"mammolapau","last":"Mammola","name":"Mammola, Stefano","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Pedro","key":"cardosopau","last":"Cardoso","name":"Cardoso, Pedro","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"David C","key":"culverpau","last":"Culver","name":"Culver, David C","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Louis","key":"deharvengpau","last":"Deharveng","name":"Deharveng, Louis","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rodrigo L","key":"ferreirapau","last":"Ferreira","name":"Ferreira, Rodrigo L","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Cene","key":"fišerpau","last":"Fišer","name":"Fišer, Cene","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Diana M P","key":"galassipau","last":"Galassi","name":"Galassi, Diana M P","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"grieblerpau","last":"Griebler","name":"Griebler, Christian","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Stuart","key":"halsepau","last":"Halse","name":"Halse, Stuart","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"William F","key":"humphreyspau","last":"Humphreys","name":"Humphreys, William F","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marco","key":"isaiapau","last":"Isaia","name":"Isaia, Marco","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Florian","key":"malardpau","last":"Malard","name":"Malard, Florian","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Alejandro","key":"martinezpau","last":"Martinez","name":"Martinez, Alejandro","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Oana T","key":"moldovanpau","last":"Moldovan","name":"Moldovan, Oana T","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Matthew L","key":"niemillerpau","last":"Niemiller","name":"Niemiller, Matthew L","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Martina","key":"pavlekpau","last":"Pavlek","name":"Pavlek, Martina","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ana Sofia P S","key":"reboleirapau","last":"Reboleira","locid":"3840f980-c12c-4d25-bb21-291ea47795c0","name":"Reboleira, Ana Sofia","name_org":"Reboleira, Ana Sofia P S","orcid":"0000-0002-4756-7034","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marconi","key":"souzasilvapau","last":"Souza-silva","name":"Souza-silva, Marconi","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Emma C","key":"teelingpau","last":"Teeling","name":"Teeling, Emma C","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"J Judson","key":"wynnepau","last":"Wynne","name":"Wynne, J Judson","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Maja","key":"zagmajsterpau","last":"Zagmajster","name":"Zagmajster, Maja","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/biosci/biz064","issn":["00063568","15253244"],"issn_org":["00063568"],"issue":"8","journal":"BioScience","pages":"641-650","status":"p","title":"BioScience","volume":"69"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85070471050"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-da8342a5-a59f-4318-9a3b-20ff2aeeb5bc"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Scientists' Warning on the Conservation of Subterranean Ecosystems","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-523942","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The real estate industry is an important indicator of national economic growth and development, which is influenced by the environment in which it operates. Various countries have been seriously affected by the most recent international financial crisis. Nevertheless, regardless of the challenges some cities currently face and the impacts on their sustainable livability, urban real estate is still of interest to investors. Given this context, researchers have sought to develop and apply methods of evaluating sustainable livability in cities. However, most practical applications have been hampered by methodological limitations (e.g., how to select and weight criteria in evaluations), which has hampered progress in this area. The present study thus aimed to develop a knowledge-based decision support system to evaluate city sustainability and livability in a transparent and informed way. To achieve its goal, this research combined cognitive mapping techniques and the analytic hierarchy process (AHP). Based on real-world data, the advantages and limitations of this integrative evaluation system are discussed.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Reis, Inês F.C.","Ferreira, Fernando A.F.","Meidutė-Kavaliauskienė, Ieva","Govindan, Kannan","Fang, Wenchang","Falcão, Pedro F."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-637553"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Govindan, Kannan"],"country":["Lithuania","Portugal","Taiwan","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lisbon University Institute","National Taipei University","The General Jonas Žemaitis Military Academy of Lithuania","University of Memphis"],"keyword":["Analytic hierarchy process AHP","Cognitive mapping","Multiple criteria decision analysis MCDA"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an evaluation thermometer for assessing city sustainability and livability","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/146646041/AN_EVALUATION_THERMOMETER_FOR_ASSESSING_CITY_SUSTAINABILITY_AND_LIVABILITY.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was partially funded by the Portuguese Foundation for Science and Technology (Grant UID/GES/00315/2013 ). Records of this study’s expert panel meetings, including photographs, software output, and non-confidential information, can be obtained from the corresponding author upon request. The authors gratefully acknowledge the outstanding contribution of the panel members: Charles Monteiro, Domitília Portela, Gonçalo Martins, Pedro Torgo, Rodrigo Avelar, and Sara Falcão. We also wish to thank the facility support provided by the ISCTE Business School, University Institute of Lisbon, Portugal."],"id":"S01-000.00-637553","identifier":[{"id":"85061795158","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-e0aa541c-52fd-4924-8509-89281043fb5d"],"keyword":["Analytic hierarchy process (AHP)","City sustainability and livability","Cognitive mapping","Multiple criteria decision analysis (MCDA)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-479B869F39CD8C439F7AFD09250F88FE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/146646041/AN_EVALUATION_THERMOMETER_FOR_ASSESSING_CITY_SUSTAINABILITY_AND_LIVABILITY.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"pt","key":"lisbon university institute","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Lisbon University I