n, Airi","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3359213","issue":"CSCW","journal":"Proc. ACM Hum. Comput. Interact.","paperid":"CSCW","status":"p","title":"Proc. ACM Hum. Comput. Interact.","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85075087505"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-930be5fb-7c55-41d1-b380-478338ad6c2a","ku-a3ebc852-8617-41b7-9056-234ac9ef75a8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"From Nomadic Work to Nomadic Leisure Practice: A Study of Long-term Bike Touring.","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-822999","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Reconstruction of Pleistocene environments and processes in the sensitive geographical location of westernmost Iberia, facing the North Atlantic Ocean, is crucial for understanding impacts on early human communities. We provide a characterization of the lowest terrace (T6) of the Lower Tejo River, at Vila Velha de Ródão (eastern central Portugal). This terrace comprises a lower gravel bed and an upper division consisting of fine to very fine sands and coarse silts. We have used a multidisciplinary approach, combining geomorphology, optically stimulated luminescence (OSL) dating, grain-size analysis and rock magnetism measurement, in order to provide new insights into the environmental changes coincident with the activity of the last Neanderthals in this region. In addition, we conducted palynological analysis, X-ray diffraction measurement and scanning electron microscopy coupled with energy dispersive spectra of the clay fraction and carbonate concretions. We discuss these new findings in the context of previously published palaeontological and archeological data. The widespread occurrence of carbonate concretions and rizoliths in the T6 profile is evidence for episodic pedogenic evaporation, in agreement with the rare occurrence and poor preservation of phytoliths. We provide updated OSL ages for the lower two Tejo terraces, obtained by post infra-red stimulated luminescence: (i) T5 is c. 140 to 70 ka; (ii) T6 is c. 60 to 35 ka. The single archaeological and fossiliferous level located at the base of the T6 upper division, recording the last regional occurrence of megafauna (elephant and rhinoceros) and Mousterian artefacts, is now dated at 44± 3 ka. With reference to the arrival of Neanderthals in the region, probably by way of the Tejo valley (from central Iberia), new dating suggests a probable age of 200-170 ka for the earliest Mousterian industry located in the topmost deposits of T4.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Cunha, Pedro P.","Martins, António A.","Buylaert, Jan Pieter","Murray, A.S.","Gouveia, Maria P.","Font, Eric","Pereira, Telmo","Figueiredo, Silvério","Ferreira, Cristiana","Bridgland, David R.","Yang, Pu","Stevaux, José C.","Mota, Rui"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-234354"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Brazil","Portugal","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Polytechnic Institute of Tomar","Universidade Federal de Mato Grosso do Sul","University of Algarve","University of Coimbra","University of Durham","University of Evora","University of Lisbon"],"keyword":["Environmental change","Late Pleistocene","OSL dating","River terraces","Western Iberia"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the lowermost tejo river terrace at foz do enxarrique portugal a palaeoenvironmental archive from c 000000000060 000000000035 ka and its implications for the last neanderthals in westernmost iberia","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/quat2010003","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-234354","identifier":[{"id":"85066785470","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-b809d655-b7e1-4501-b7f9-be35f3e437bf"],"keyword":["Environmental change","Late Pleistocene","OSL dating","River terraces","Western Iberia"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-22DA67649095275D91C36CEB49E40313"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/quat2010003","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"pt","key":"university of coimbra","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Coimbra","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"pt","key":"university of evora","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Evora","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Geoscience","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Geoscience, Department of Geoscience - Nordic Laboratory for Luminescence Dating"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"pt","key":"university of lisbon","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Lisbon","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"pt","key":"university of algarve","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Algarve","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"pt","key":"polytechnic institute of tomar","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Polytechnic Institute of Tomar","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"gb","key":"university of durham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Durham","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"br","key":"universidade federal de mato grosso do sul","loc":["Brazil","America, South"],"name":"Universidade Federal de Mato Grosso do Sul","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro P.","key":"cunhapau","last":"Cunha","name":"Cunha, Pedro P.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"António A.","key":"martinspau","last":"Martins","name":"Martins, António A.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan Pieter","key":"buylaertpau","last":"Buylaert","name":"Buylaert, Jan Pieter","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andrew S.","key":"murraypau","last":"Murray","locid":"559f8eee-6799-4f40-ac31-7dc594ce950f","name":"Murray, A.S.","name_org":"Murray, Andrew S.","orcid":"0000-0001-5559-1862","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria P.","key":"gouveiapau","last":"Gouveia","name":"Gouveia, Maria P.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Eric","key":"fontpau","last":"Font","name":"Font, Eric","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Telmo","key":"pereirapau","last":"Pereira","name":"Pereira, Telmo","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Silvério","key":"figueiredopau","last":"Figueiredo","name":"Figueiredo, Silvério","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Cristiana","key":"ferreirapau","last":"Ferreira","name":"Ferreira, Cristiana","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"David R.","key":"bridglandpau","last":"Bridgland","name":"Bridgland, David R.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pu","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Pu","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"José C.","key":"stevauxpau","last":"Stevaux","name":"Stevaux, José C.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rui","key":"motapau","last":"Mota","name":"Mota, Rui","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/quat2010003","issn":["2571550X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Quaternary","paperid":"3","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute (MDPI)","status":"p","title":"Quaternary","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85066785470"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b809d655-b7e1-4501-b7f9-be35f3e437bf"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The lowermost Tejo river terrace at Foz do Enxarrique, Portugal : A palaeoenvironmental archive from c. 60-35 ka and its implications for the last neanderthals in westernmost iberia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-234354","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background: No data exist about the characteristics of infective endocarditis (IE) post-transcatheter aortic valve replacement (TAVR) according to transcatheter valve type. We aimed to determine the incidence, clinical characteristics, and outcomes of patients with IE post-TAVR treated with balloon-expandable valve (BEV) versus self-expanding valve (SEV) systems. Methods: Data from the multicenter Infectious Endocarditis After TAVR International Registry was used to compare IE patients with BEV versus SEV. Results: A total of 245 patients with IE post-TAVR were included (SEV, 47%; BEV, 53%). The timing between TAVR and IE was similar between groups (SEV, 5.5 [1.2-15] months versus BEV, 5.3 [1.7-11.4] months; P=0.89). Enterococcal IE was more frequent in the SEV group (36.5% versus 15.4%; P<0.01), and vegetation location differed according to valve type (stent frame, SEV, 18.6%; BEV, 6.9%; P=0.01; valve leaflet, SEV, 23.9%; BEV, 38.5%; P=0.01). BEV recipients had a higher rate of stroke/systemic embolism (20.0% versus 8.7%, adjusted OR: 2.46, 95% CI: 1.04-5.82, P=0.04). Surgical explant of the transcatheter valve (SEV, 8.7%; BEV, 13.8%; P=0.21), and in-hospital death at the time of IE episode (SEV, 35.6%; BEV, 37.7%; P=0.74) were similar between groups. After a mean follow-up of 13±12 months, 59.1% and 54.6% of the SEV and BEV recipients, respectively, had died (P=0.66). Conclusions: The characteristics of IE post-TAVR, including microorganism type, vegetation location, and embolic complications but not early or late mortality, differed according to valve type. These results may help to guide the diagnosis and management of IE and inform future research studies in the field.","author_count":64,"contributors":["Regueiro, Ander","Linke, Axel","Latib, Azeem","Ihlemann, Nikolaj","Urena, Marina","Walther, Thomas","Husser, Oliver","Herrmann, Howard C.","Nombela-Franco, Luis","Cheema, Asim","Le Breton, Hervé","Stortecky, Stefan","Kapadia, Samir","Bartorelli, An