ast":"Rodés-Cabau","name":"Rodés-Cabau, Josep","rank":65,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27623462"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1001/jama.2016.12347","issn":["00987484","01851160"],"issn_org":["00987484"],"issue":"10","journal":"JAMA  The Journal of the American Medical Association","pages":"1083-1092","status":"p","title":"JAMA  The Journal of the American Medical Association","title_org":"J A M A: The Journal of the American Medical Association","volume":"316"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84988020948"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d9abaf1a-de9a-42be-8bbf-2593956659e6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Association Between Transcatheter Aortic Valve Replacement and Subsequent Infective Endocarditis and In-Hospital Death","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-523470","year":"2016","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This study investigated the effects of seaweed dietary supplementation on measures of fish performance including aerobic metabolism, digestive enzymes activity, innate immune status, oxidative damage, and growth rate using European seabass (Dicentrarchus labrax). Fish were fed for 49 days with three different diets: a control diet (CTRL), a Gracilaria-supplemented diet (GR7.5), and a mixed diet (Mix) composed of Gracilaria, Fucus, and Ulva genera representatives. All diets were isoenergetic (22 kJ g −1 adjusted for dry matter (DM)), isoproteic (47 %DM), and isolipidic (18 %DM) and tested in triplicate groups of 20 fish (initial body weight 25.5 ± 4.1 g). Final results showed similar growth rates and digestive activities between diets. Maximum and standard metabolic rates and aerobic metabolic scope revealed comparable results for the three diets. In contrast, fish fed with GR7.5 exhibited elevated routine metabolic rate (190.7 mg O 2 kg −1 h −1). Fish fed with the GR7.5 and Mix diets had lower alternative complement pathway (ACH50) (62.5 and 63 units mL −1 respectively) than CTRL (84 units mL −1) GR7.5 increased lipid peroxidation and cholinesterase levels, as well as glutathione s-transferase activity. Mix diet increased glutathione reductase activity when compared to CTRL. Collectively, our findings suggest that dietary seaweed supplementation may alter seabass metabolic rate, innate immune, and antioxidant responses without compromising growth parameters.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Peixoto, Maria João","Svendsen, Jon Christian","Malte, Hans","Pereira, Luis Ferreira Pereira","Carvalho, Pedro Carvalho","Pereira, Rui Pereira","Gonçalves, José Fernando Gonçalves","Ozório, Rodrigo Otávio Ozório"],"cuid":["S02-095.12-016837"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Portugal"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Porto"],"keyword":["Digestive enzymes","Growth rate","Innate immune response","Metabolic rate","Oxidative stress","Seaweeds"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diets supplemented with seaweed affect metabolic rate innate immune and antioxidant responses but not individual growth rate in european seabass dicentrarchus labrax","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84945570387","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-095.12-016837","identifier":[{"id":"84945570387","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-390d83aa-323b-495d-ae55-4e563fbf2e55","dtu-b9c3b32d-4ded-462f-b3ff-16a8ec35914d"],"keyword":["Digestive enzymes","Growth rate","Innate immune response","Metabolic rate","Oxidative stress","Seaweeds"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7A5CCA86442DEEBFCEE019D5FE7878FF"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"pt","key":"university of porto","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Porto","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources","Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources, Section for Ecosystem based Marine Management","Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources, Section for Freshwater Fisher