url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-471638","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"In recent years, there have been several attempts to improve the diagnosis of infection caused by Helicobacter pylori. Fluorescence in situ hybridization (FISH) is a commonly used technique to detect H. pylori infection but it requires biopsies from the stomach. Thus, the development of an in vivo FISH-based method (FIVH) that directly detects and allows the visualization of the bacterium within the human body would significantly reduce the time of analysis, allowing the diagnosis to be performed during endoscopy. In a previous study we designed and synthesized a phosphorothioate locked nucleic acid (LNA)/ 2' O-methyl RNA (2'OMe) probe using standard phosphoramidite chemistry and FISH hybridization was then successfully performed both on adhered and suspended bacteria at 37°C. In this work we simplified, shortened and adapted FISH to work at gastric pH values, meaning that the hybridization step now takes only 30 minutes and, in addition to the buffer, uses only urea and probe at non-toxic concentrations. Importantly, the sensitivity and specificity of the FISH method was maintained in the range of conditions tested, even at low stringency conditions (e.g., low pH). In conclusion, this methodology is a promising approach that might be used in vivo in the future in combination with a confocal laser endomicroscope for H. pylori visualization.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Fontenete, Sílvia","Leite, Marina","Guimarães, Nuno","Madureira, Pedro","Ferreira, Rui Manuel","Figueiredo, Céu","Wengel, Jesper","Azevedo, Nuno Filipe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-593858"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Portugal"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Porto"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards fluorescence in vivo hybridization fivh detection of h pylori in gastric mucosa using advanced lna probes","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/116660591/Towards_fluorescence_in_vivo_hybridization_FIVH_detection_of_H._pylori_in_Gastric_Mucosa_using_advanced_LNA_probes..pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-593858","identifier":[{"id":"25915865","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84928573017","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC4410960","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-47de6678-a9db-476b-a5c7-fa59cafc9baf"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2773DC8319D3CC1776E7566988D0869B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/116660591/Towards_fluorescence_in_vivo_hybridization_FIVH_detection_of_H._pylori_in_Gastric_Mucosa_using_advanced_LNA_probes..pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0125494","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Physics, Chemistry and Pharmacy, Nucleic Acid Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"pt","key":"university of porto","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Porto","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sílvia","key":"fontenetepau","last":"Fontenete","locid":"a9154e5e-0c8b-4f89-a0e9-f036a70a9af0","name":"Fontenete, Sílvia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marina","key":"leitepau","last":"Leite","name":"Leite, Marina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nuno","key":"guimarãespau","last":"Guimarães","locid":"8d51836e-490b-4b63-bee5-b779a6d2f448","name":"Guimarães, Nuno","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro","key":"madureirapau","last":"Madureira","name":"Madureira, Pedro","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Rui Manuel","key":"ferreirapau","last":"Ferreira","name":"Ferreira, Rui Manuel","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Céu","key":"figueiredopau","last":"Figueiredo","name":"Figueiredo, Céu","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"wengelpau","last":"Wengel","locid":"4803676b-fbaf-4593-baab-147b5465bbec","name":"Wengel, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-9835-1009","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Nuno Filipe","key":"azevedopau","last":"Azevedo","name":"Azevedo, Nuno Filipe","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25915865"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0125494","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"4","journal":"PLOS ONE","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84928573017"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-47de6678-a9db-476b-a5c7-fa59cafc9baf"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Towards Fluorescence In Vivo Hybridization (FIVH) Detection of H. pylori in Gastric Mucosa Using Advanced LNA Probes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-593858","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"This work presents the results of measuring pH, sugars, and anthocyanin content of whole grape berries. The spectrum of each sample, composed of six whole grape berries, was collected using hyperspectral imaging in reflectance mode from 380 to 1028 nm. The spectra were converted to enological parameters by multilayer perceptrons created using 240 samples that were split for 7-fold cross-validation and test. The test set with 30 samples revealed R2 values of 0.73, 0.92 and 0.95 and RMSE of 0.18, 0.95 °Brix and 14 mg/l for pH, sugars and anthocyanin content, respectively. This is the only work, up to the authors’ knowledge, that reports the simultaneous determination of pH, sugars and anthocyanin with a spatial resolution smaller than the bunch size, by spectroscopy measurements done in reflectance mode. The results presented show an improvement of the state-of-the-art, for both reflectance and transmittance mode, that is particularly notorious for anthocyanin measurement.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Fernandes, Armando M.","Franco de los Ríos, Camilo","Mendes-Ferreira, Ana","Mendes-Faia, Arlete","Leal da Costa, Pedro","Melo-Pinto, Pedro"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-506713"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Portugal"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","UTAD/CITAB","Universidade de Trás-os-Montes e Alto Douro","University of Lisbon"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"brix ph and anthocyanin content determination in whole port wine grape berries by hyperspectral imaging and neural networks","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-506713","identifier":[{"id":"84930667884","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-bdc6a3d9-bad1-4dd0-a052-243c021c72be"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5A8554750890389E91655168D2E4B291"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"pt","key":"university of lisbon","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Lisbon","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food and Resource Economics, Section for Production, Markets and Policy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"pt","key":"universidade de trás os montes e alto douro","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Universidade de Trás-os-Montes e Alto Douro","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"pt","key":"utad citab","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"UTAD/CITAB","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Armando M.","key":"fernandespau","last":"Fernandes","name":"Fernandes, Armando M.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Camilo","key":"francopau","last":"Franco","locid":"a2faf04d-be2c-4a24-a641-9a234c490ff8","name":"Franco de los Ríos, Camilo","name_org":"Franco, Camilo","orcid":"0000-0002-2006-3821","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Ana","key":"mendesferreirapau","last":"Mendes-Ferreira","name":"Mendes-Ferreira, Ana","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Arlete","key":"mendesfaiapau","last":"Mendes-Faia","name":"Mendes-Faia, Arlete","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Pedro","key":"lealdacostapau","last":"Leal da Costa","name":"Leal da Costa, Pedro","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Pedro","key":"melopintopau","last":"Melo-Pinto","name":"Melo-Pinto, Pedro","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.compag.2015.05.013","issn":["01681699","18727107"],"issn_org":["01681699"],"journal":"Computers and Electronics in Agriculture","pages":"88-96","status":"p","title":"Computers and Electronics in Agriculture","volume":"115"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84930667884"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-bdc6a3d9-bad1-4dd0-a052-243c021c72be"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Brix, pH and anthocyanin content determination in whole Port wine grape berries by hyperspectral imaging and neural networks","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-506713","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The cis-regulatory effects responsible for cancer development have not been as extensively studied as the perturbations of the protein coding genome in tumorigenesis. To better characterize colorectal cancer (CRC) development we conducted an RNA-sequencing experiment of 103 matched tumour and normal colon mucosa samples from Danish CRC patients, 90 of which were germline-genotyped. By investigating allele-specific expression (ASE) we show that the germline genotypes remain important determinants of allelic gene expression in tumours. Using the changes in ASE in matched pairs of samples we discover 71 genes with excess of somatic cis-regulatory effects in CRC, suggesting a cancer driver role. We correlate genotypes and gene expression to identify expression quantitative trait loci (eQTLs) and find 1,693 and 948 eQTLs in normal samples and tumours, respectively. We estimate that 36% of the tumour eQTLs are exclusive to CRC and show that this specificity is partially driven by increased expression of specific transcription factors and changes in methylation patterns. We show that tumour-specific eQTLs are more enriched for low CRC genome-wide association study (GWAS) P values than shared eQTLs, which suggests that some of the GWAS variants are tumour specific regulatory variants. Importantly, tumour-specific eQTL genes also accumulate more somatic mutations when compared to the shared eQTL genes, raising the possibility that they constitute germline-derived cancer regulatory drivers. Collectively the integration of genome and the transcriptome reveals a substantial number of putative somatic and germline cis-regulatory cancer changes that may have a role in tumorigenesis.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Ongen, Halit","Andersen, Claus Lindbjerg","Bramsen, Jesper Bertram","Oster, Bodil","Rasmussen, Mads Heilskov","Ferreira, Pedro G","Sandoval, Juan","Vidal, Enrique","Whiffin, Nicola","Planchon, Alexandra","Padioleau, Ismael","Bielser, Deborah","Romano, Luciana","Tomlinson, Ian","Houlston, Richard S","Esteller, Manel","Ørntoft, Torben Falck","Dermitzakis, Emmanouil T"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-146700"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Spain","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bellvitge Biomedical Research Institute","ICREA","Institute of Cancer Research","University of Barcelona","University of Geneva"],"keyword":["Alleles","Cell Transformation Neoplastic","Colorectal Neoplasms","DNA methylation","Gene Expression Profiling","Gene Expression Regulation Neoplastic","Genes Neoplasm","Genome Wide Association Study","Genotype","Germ Line Mutation","Humans","Intestinal Mucosa","Quantitative Trait Loci","Regulatory Sequences Nucleic Acid","Sequence Analysis RNA","Transcription Factors","Transcriptome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"putative cis regulatory drivers in colorectal cancer","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/nature13602","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-146700","identifier":[{"id":"84905581513","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25079323","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-1e535abb-959e-446a-8830-8dbb15f346bb"],"keyword":["Alleles","Cell Transformation, Neoplastic","Colorectal Neoplasms","DNA Methylation","Gene Expression Profiling","Gene Expression Regulation, Neoplastic","Genes, Neoplasm","Genome-Wide Association Study","Genotype","Germ-Line Mutation","Humans","Intestinal Mucosa","Quantitative Trait Loci","Regulatory Sequences, Nucleic Acid","Sequence Analysis, RNA","Transcription Factors","Transcriptome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1A412DEB889B3D0A765EFCC12C378C59"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/nature13602","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ch","key":"university of geneva","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Geneva","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Molecular Medicine (MOMA)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital (AUH)"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"es","key":"bellvitge biomedical research institute","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Bellvitge Biomedical Research Institute","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"institute of cancer research","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Institute of Cancer Research","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"es","key":"university of barcelona","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Barcelona","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"es","key":"icrea","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"ICREA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Halit","key":"ongenpau","last":"Ongen","name":"Ongen, Halit","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus Lindbjerg","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"f97421ce-9c23-4c51-9fcd-be0843ed0c0f","name":"Andersen, Claus Lindbjerg","orcid":"0000-0002-7406-2103","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper B","key":"bramsenpau","last":"Bramsen","locid":"bcaa0339-abb7-415d-9fd3-bff68766370e","name":"Bramsen, Jesper Bertram","name_org":"Bramsen, Jesper B","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Bodil","key":"osterpau","last":"Oster","name":"Oster, Bodil","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads H","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"3285e14f-ef19-480d-97ff-c95d6a90b354","name":"Rasmussen, Mads Heilskov","name_org":"Rasmussen, Mads H","orcid":"0000-0001-5723-6303","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro G","key":"ferreirapau","last":"Ferreira","name":"Ferreira, Pedro G","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan","key":"sandovalpau","last":"Sandoval","name":"Sandoval, Juan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Enrique","key":"vidalpau","last":"Vidal","name":"Vidal, Enrique","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicola","key":"whiffinpau","last":"Whiffin","name":"Whiffin, Nicola","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexandra","key":"planchonpau","last":"Planchon","name":"Planchon, Alexandra","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ismael","key":"padioleaupau","last":"Padioleau","name":"Padioleau, Ismael","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Deborah","key":"bielserpau","last":"Bielser","name":"Bielser, Deborah","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luciana","key":"romanopau","last":"Romano","name":"Romano, Luciana","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Ian","key":"tomlinsonpau","last":"Tomlinson","name":"Tomlinson, Ian","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Richard S","key":"houlstonpau","last":"Houlston","name":"Houlston, Richard S","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 7 8","corresponding":null,"first":"Manel","key":"estellerpau","last":"Esteller","name":"Esteller, Manel","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben F","key":"orntoftpau","last":"Orntoft","locid":"37db9bb8-c48f-42aa-947f-23679e86c464","name":"Ørntoft, Torben Falck","name_org":"Orntoft, Torben F","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Emmanouil T","key":"dermitzakispau","last":"Dermitzakis","name":"Dermitzakis, Emmanouil T","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25079323"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/nature13602","issn":["00280836","14764687"],"issn_org":["00280836"],"issue":"7512","journal":"Nature","pages":"87-90","publisher":"Springer Nature","status":"p","title":"Nature","volume":"512"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84905581513"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1e535abb-959e-446a-8830-8dbb15f346bb"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Putative cis-regulatory drivers in colorectal cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-146700","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The fifth Millennium Development Goal (MDG 5) established the goal of a 75% reduction in the maternal mortality ratio (MMR; number of maternal deaths per 100,000 livebirths) between 1990 and 2015. We aimed to measure levels and track trends in maternal mortality, the key causes contributing to maternal death, and timing of maternal death with respect to delivery. METHODS: We used robust statistical methods including the Cause of Death Ensemble model (CODEm) to analyse a database of data for 7065 site-years and estimate the number of maternal deaths from all causes in 188 countries between 1990 and 2013. We estimated the number of pregnancy-related deaths caused by HIV on the basis of a systematic review of the relative risk of dying during pregnancy for HIV-positive women compared with HIV-negative women. We also estimated the fraction of these deaths aggravated by pregnancy on the basis of a systematic review. To estimate the numbers of maternal deaths due to nine different causes, we identified 61 sources from a systematic review and 943 site-years of vital registration data. We also did a systematic review of reports about the timing of maternal death, identifying 142 sources to use in our analysis. We developed estimates for each country for 1990-2013 using Bayesian meta-regression. We estimated 95% uncertainty intervals (UIs) for all values. FINDINGS: 292,982 (95% UI 261,017-327,792) maternal deaths occurred in 2013, compared with 376,034 (343,483-407,574) in 1990. The global annual rate of change in the MMR was -0·3% (-1·1 to 0·6) from 1990 to 2003, and -2·7% (-3·9 to -1·5) from 2003 to 2013, with evidence of continued acceleration. MMRs reduced consistently in south, east, and southeast Asia between 1990 and 2013, but maternal deaths increased in much of sub-Saharan Africa during the 1990s. 2070 (1290-2866) maternal deaths were related to HIV in 2013, 0·4% (0·2-0·6) of the global total. MMR was highest in the oldest age groups in both 1990 and 2013. In 2013, most deaths occurred intrapartum or postpartum. Causes varied by region and between 1990 and 2013. We recorded substantial variation in the MMR by country in 2013, from 956·8 (685·1-1262·8) in South Sudan to 2·4 (1·6-3·6) in Iceland. INTERPRETATION: Global rates of change suggest that only 16 countries will achieve the MDG 5 target by 2015. Accelerated reductions since the Millennium Declaration in 2000 coincide with increased development assistance for maternal, newborn, and child health. Setting of targets and associated interventions for after 2015 will need careful consideration of regions that are making slow progress, such as west and central Africa. FUNDING: Bill & Melinda Gates Foundation.","author_count":349,"contributors":["Kassebaum, Nicholas J","Bertozzi-Villa, Amelia","Coggeshall, Megan S","Shackelford, Katya A","Steiner, Caitlyn","Heuton, Kyle R","Gonzalez-Medina, Diego","Barber, Ryan","Huynh, Chantal","Dicker, Daniel","Templin, Tara","Wolock, Timothy M","Ozgoren, Ayse Abbasoglu","Abd-Allah, Foad","Abera, Semaw Ferede","Abubakar, Ibrahim","Achoki, Tom","Adelekan, Ademola","Ademi, Zanfina","Adou, Arsène Kouablan","Adsuar, José C","Agardh, Emilie E","Akena, Dickens","Alasfoor, Deena","Alemu, Zewdie Aderaw","Alfonso-Cristancho, Rafael","Alhabib, Samia","Ali, Raghib","Al Kahbouri, Mazin J","Alla, François","Allen, Peter J","AlMazroa, Mohammad A","Alsharif, Ubai","Alvarez, Elena","Alvis-Guzmán, Nelson","Amankwaa, Adansi A","Amare, Azmeraw T","Amini, Hassan","Ammar, Walid","Antonio, Carl A T","Anwari, Palwasha","Arnlöv, Johan","Arsenijevic, Valentina S Arsic","Artaman, Ali","Asad, Majed Masoud","Asghar, Rana J","Assadi, Reza","Atkins, Lydia S","Badawi, Alaa","Balakrishnan, Kalpana","Basu, Arindam","Basu, Sanjay","Beardsley, Justin","Bedi, Neeraj","Bekele, Tolesa","Bell, Michelle L","Bernabe, Eduardo","Beyene, Tariku J","Bhutta, Zulfiqar","Bin Abdulhak, Aref","Blore, Jed D","Basara, Berrak Bora","Bose, Dipan","Breitborde, Nicholas","C